WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.409
The desert is still.

00:00:02.409 --> 00:00:09.120
The night seems endless, silent, and at peace…
until it’s pierced by the sound of gunshots

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.219
and screams.

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:16.880
Deep in the Sahara, the SCP Foundation is
waging war against a newly discovered enemy.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.700
A squad of foundation agents is retreating,
trying to get away from the ones who massacred

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.520
their allies.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.100
They were attempting to eliminate the threat
using conventional means, but their rifles

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.379
were no match for the reality bending entities
of the Kingdom of Abaddon.

00:00:33.379 --> 00:00:36.989
The retreating agents cover one another as
they make their way back to the extraction

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:37.989
point.

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:39.809
The enemy force advances.

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:44.039
Agents that are caught too close to the sorcerers
of Abaddon disintegrate into thin air.

00:00:44.039 --> 00:00:46.370
This is not an enemy they can defeat.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:52.040
The SCP agents need to get back to base and
relay what they have found to their superiors.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:56.319
Out of the hundreds of agents sent into the
Sahara that night, only a handful make it

00:00:56.319 --> 00:00:57.570
out alive.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.800
They are debriefed by their superiors at the
Foundation who classify the anomalous humanoids

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.929
under the highest of threat levels.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:06.610
The Kingdom of Abaddon is a threat.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:11.050
The Kingdom of Abaddon must be eliminated.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:14.310
Reconnaissance done prior to the disastrous
mission had alerted the Foundation to the

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:19.000
presence of anomalies in the region, but they
had no idea how strong the anomalous humanoids

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.130
would be.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:24.450
From data gathered through old reports, it
seemed that the Abaddon humanoids were responsible

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:30.180
for the deaths of no fewer than 75 Foundation
personnel, and had stolen at least 12 different

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.350
items from the Foundation.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:37.250
The leaders of the SCP Foundation tasked research
team Omega-5 with developing a weapon that

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:41.180
would be capable of destroying the Kingdom
of Abaddon once and for all.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:45.869
The weapon they are researching must be capable
of long range destruction, because the moment

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:50.470
any Foundation agent gets close to the area,
they are vaporized by the reality manipulating

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:55.659
powers of its inhabitants The project is given
the name “Twins of God” and is led by

00:01:55.659 --> 00:01:59.689
a Foundation doctor known only by the designation
“O5-1.”

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:06.020
O5-1 is popular in the SCP Foundation, well
known for his in-depth research and charismatic

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.149
personality, making him the perfect person
to lead such a project.

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:15.360
And O5-1 recently came across an anomaly that
he believes holds the solution the Foundation

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.560
has been looking for to defeat the Kingdom
of Abaddon…

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.069
Item-001.And so the Omega-5 team gets to work.

00:02:23.069 --> 00:02:27.510
They discover that the anomaly has incredible
powers when put inside a host, which they

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:32.320
refer to as an Item-001 entity, and set up
a series of experiments using different people

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.260
to harness its energy The first series of
tests all end in tragedy.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.810
The anomaly causes the entity it inhabits
to become intensely radioactive.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:47.239
Anyone who gets close to it succumbs to immediate
radiation sickness, and eventually death.

00:02:47.239 --> 00:02:51.560
To stop the radiation problems the Omega-5
research group intensifies the containment

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.560
procedures.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.730
O5-1 receives reports from the higher ups
that the Kingdom of Abaddon has attacked another

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.040
Foundation facility in Sudan.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.560
Long-range defense is needed A.S.A.P.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:07.290
The administrator puts more pressure on Omega-5,
and especially its leader O5-1, to solve the

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:12.111
problems of Item-001 and develop a weapon
that can save the Foundation.

00:03:12.111 --> 00:03:17.099
He stays awake for days on end, working tirelessly
to create a safe and controllable Item-001

00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:18.819
entity.

00:03:18.819 --> 00:03:23.549
Although there are signs that the weapon will
work, it is still unpredictable.

00:03:23.549 --> 00:03:29.629
When Item-001 is initiated, the host entity
becomes paralyzed, suffers severe cerebral

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:34.409
hemorrhaging, and soon a new host is needed
before testing can begin again.

00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:37.670
And that’s not the only thing going wrong.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:42.390
Whenever the anomaly is put into a new host,
sudden and random destruction of on-site structures

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.330
and personnel takes place.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:48.799
O5-1 knows though, that if this power can
be harnessed and controlled in the right way,

00:03:48.799 --> 00:03:52.959
that it could be the weapon that the Foundation
needs to wipe out the Kingdom of Abaddon once

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:54.340
and for all.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:04:00.840
In order to control Item-001, O5-1 has a mind-kill
switch implanted in its hosts’ brains.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:06.560
O5-1 can activate the implant to incapacitate
the host and immediately stop the unwanted

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.560
destruction.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:11.469
Countless hosts are terminated by this mind-kill
switch in the early trials conducted by the

00:04:11.469 --> 00:04:17.910
Omega-5 team, but progress continues to be
made and eventually a hypothesis is formulated.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:22.729
Perhaps the disastrous side effects of Item-001
can be offset by spreading the anomaly across

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:24.180
multiple subjects.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:28.630
They theorize that the immense mental load
of the anomaly can be distributed among several

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:33.620
hosts, thus reducing the toll it takes on
each and giving them the ability to control

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.960
its immense power.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:41.370
But O5-1 and the Omega-5 team need more data,
and for that, they need more bodies.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:45.810
They consult with the director of Site-17
and it is concluded that the nearby town of

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:50.740
San Marco would be an appropriate place to
get the additional test subjects they require.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:56.330
On a quiet Sunday morning, Omega-5 along with
support from a squad of armed SCP agents storm

00:04:56.330 --> 00:05:00.270
into the San Marcos de la Vida Sterna Church
during the middle of mass.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:04.770
They gather up a number of the younger congregants
and bring them back to the site where Item-001

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.419
is housed.

00:05:06.419 --> 00:05:11.150
The researchers quickly ran through their
new supply of test subjects though, and Omega-5

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:15.350
would need to get even more if their research
was to continue.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:20.150
Instead of going back and forth between the
testing facility and San Marco, O5-1 decides

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:24.150
to move the entire Item-001 operation to the
town itself.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:30.250
He renames the town, Testing Site-001, and
Omega-5 rounds up 23 of the healthiest subjects

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:34.010
they can find for use in the next series of
research tests.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:38.680
A few weeks after occupying the town of San
Marco, Omega-5 makes it’s most substantial

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.380
progress yet.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:45.210
Just as they theorized, by spreading out the
anomaly of Item-001 across a specific group

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.970
of hosts, they can control its powers.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:52.610
The tests may have cost the lives of almost
everyone in the town, but the ends certainly

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.539
justify the means.

00:05:54.539 --> 00:05:59.250
The Kingdom of Abaddon poses an existential
threat to the SCP Foundation after all, and

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:04.009
thanks to this research they will soon have
a weapon capable of bringing them victory.

00:06:04.009 --> 00:06:10.090
The Foundation administrator criticizes O5-1’s
methods, but can’t argue with his results.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.020
Unfortunately, O5-1 has a dark secret.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:17.449
A secret that disturbs even the most hardened
and loyal members of Omega-5.

00:06:17.449 --> 00:06:21.919
A secret that has to do with the Item-001
hosts.

00:06:21.919 --> 00:06:27.190
The hosts that Omega-5 has made its major
progress with are not the ordinary test subjects

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.599
normally used by the Foundation.

00:06:29.599 --> 00:06:35.130
No, the test subjects O5-1 makes his breakthrough
with… are children.

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:39.889
Nine of them to be exact, all between four
and eleven years old.

00:06:39.889 --> 00:06:44.870
Despite being told specifically by the Foundation
administrator to only test on adults, the

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:50.150
research required O5-1 to break the chain
of command and follow the science down the

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.340
path it led.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:55.900
The children are contained in a reinforced
bunker where only O5-1, and a select few,

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.110
have access.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:00.860
They are technically alive, but are functionally
brain dead.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:06.490
The group of nine children share a hive mind
that can process information, and more importantly,

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:12.160
can unleash the full potential of the implanted
anomaly, creating and controlling a devastating

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.390
power.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:16.300
But not everyone is thrilled with what they’ve
achieved.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:19.760
Members of Omega-5 are haunted by the screams
of the children that they’ve forced to be

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:21.949
part of their weapon development program.

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:27.199
They describe their merging with Item-001
as being a process that rips out their souls

00:07:27.199 --> 00:07:30.919
and replaces them with something much more
sinister.

00:07:30.919 --> 00:07:37.050
In fact all of Omega-5 regret what they have
been a part of and what they’ve done, all

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.479
except O5-1.

00:07:39.479 --> 00:07:44.460
The nine children can channel unprecedented
amounts of energy from an unknown origin that

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:50.870
Omega-5 hypothesizes comes from an extradimensional
source, which is then used to unbind atoms

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.270
at the quantum level.

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:56.680
When the right activation words are spoken,
it appears as though this tremendous power

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:01.400
gives the children the ability to annihilate
anything in the entire universe.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.789
It’s the gun to end all guns.

00:08:04.789 --> 00:08:08.889
And only O5-1 has the key to control it.

00:08:08.889 --> 00:08:14.169
The nine children work so well within Item-001
that Omega-5 reclassifies it to include the

00:08:14.169 --> 00:08:16.340
nine children themselves.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:24.009
They are not just the entity housing or controlling
Item-001, they permanently become Item-001.

00:08:24.009 --> 00:08:28.530
Once Omega-5 has a better understanding of
Item-001, they begin to run tests to find

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:31.130
out the full extent of its abilities.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.540
First they test the distance Item-001 can
reach.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:38.930
The initial test that Omega-5 carries out
is on a steel rod placed 5 kilometers away.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:42.350
O5-1 orders the children to destroy the target.

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:45.820
Moments later the phone next to O5-1 begins
to ring.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:49.700
When he picks it up the observer tasked with
watching the pole is on the other end.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:53.620
He informs O5-1 that the steel rod has been
completely vaporized.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.850
O5-1 is not satisfied though.

00:08:55.850 --> 00:09:01.350
He has another pole set out, this time placed
8,000 kilometers away from the nine children.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:05.180
O5-1 asks the children to destroy that rod.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.790
Almost immediately, the phone rings again.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:10.040
The target has been vaporized.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.580
O5-1 smiles.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:17.830
The next series of tests Omega-5 runs on Item-001
are to determine the maximum size of an object

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.250
that can be destroyed.

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:24.160
The tests start out with a steel sphere, 3
meters in diameter, placed 1,000 kilometers

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.160
from Item-001.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:28.560
O5-1 orders the children to destroy the object.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.550
It is instantly vaporized.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:33.270
O5-1 has seen enough small tests.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:35.780
It’s time for something big.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:39.840
So he does something that will later be questioned
by everyone at the SCP Foundation.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:45.710
He orders the nine children to destroy a Church
of the Broken God worship site in Turkey.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:50.860
Not long after the destruction order is given
to Item-001, reports begin coming in.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:56.430
The worship site has been obliterated with
no observable damage to the surrounding area.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:58.400
Deadly and precise.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:01.310
O5-1 closes his eyes and takes a deep breath.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:05.120
He looks as if he is overcome by an immense
spiritual experience.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:09.930
He opens his eyes, leans over to the children,
and whispers the name of someone.

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:15.040
Later that day, O5-1 finds out that the target
he had named has been vaporized.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:20.350
The success of Omega-5 and Item-001 is relayed
to the administration of the Foundation.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:25.780
They are so impressed that they make plans
to use Item-001 to eliminate the Abaddon threat

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:27.570
once and for all.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:32.850
However, one of the heads of the foundation,
Administrator Williams, has major concerns

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:35.870
about the way O5-1 is running the program.

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:42.240
The updates that O5-1 has been sending have
become less scientific, and more philosophical…

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:45.940
more… spiritual.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:50.300
Administrator Williams sends a letter to O5-1
reassuring him that he is doing good work,

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:55.380
but once the mission to destroy the Kingdom
of Abaddon is completed, O5-1 will be promoted

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:58.570
to director, and reassigned to the newly constructed
Site-19.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:05.240
For the good of the Foundation, and maybe
the world, he’ll be permanently moved away

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:06.240
from Item-001.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:13.080
O5-1’s response is short and to the point,
“I am fine, Administrator.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.640
The project is finished.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:18.440
We will complete our task when you arrive.”

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:21.760
Administrator Williams arrives at Site-001
a few days later.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.450
He is greeted by O5-1 and the Omega-5 team.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:29.180
Williams can’t help but notice that O5-1
has a strange look in his eyes.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:35.600
It is the look of a crazed man who has been
lost in his work, and who has, perhaps, lost

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:37.130
himself.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:41.870
Williams puts the thought away though and
walks with O5-1 and his accompanying agents

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:47.330
to the viewing area where the powers of Item-001
will be demonstrated.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:52.000
Administrator Williams and the other agents
watch from a protected viewing room as O5-1

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.560
enters the chamber of his new super weapon.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:59.200
It’s time to see if their weapon that has
had so much time, effort, sweat, tears, and

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:03.690
especially blood poured into it, will have
been worth it.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:07.991
Everyone watches as O5-1 leans over and says
the name of the Abaddon Citadel to the nine

00:12:07.991 --> 00:12:09.340
children.

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:11.380
All at once, they start to glow.

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:15.830
No one observing can see what has happened
in the far off Kingdom, but they know something

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.060
big has happened.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:20.660
The administrator is thrilled, but notices
something.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:24.700
O5-1 hesitated a moment while leaning over
the children before standing back up.

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:27.460
Did he whisper something else to them?

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:31.940
And then Administrator Williams vaporizes,
pulled apart at an atomic level before he

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.520
has the chance to scream.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.140
What’s going on?

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:39.000
The agents standing next to where Administrator
Williams previously existed begin to yell

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.400
and pull out their guns.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.110
They burst through the door of the observation
room and run down the hallway towards where

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:47.030
O5-1 and the nine children are located.

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.560
The armed agents rush into the room, but O5-1
is gone.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:53.770
The nine children are still.

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:58.960
Over the next few weeks O5-1 is reported to
be seen several times by SCP agents.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:02.820
However, no one is able to catch him, and
it appears as though other members of the

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:08.000
SCP Foundation have also gone AWOL as well,
perhaps joining him on the run.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:12.510
It is unclear what his plan is, but reports
from the reconnaissance team sent into the

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:17.180
Sahara make it obvious what the result of
his first command to the children was.

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:20.830
There isn’t a single humanoid or building
left in the Kingdom of Abaddon.

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:26.800
But even with this victory, the highest levels
of the SCP Foundation have an ominous thought

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.010
lurking in the back of their minds.

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:32.630
Where did O5-1 go, and what is he planning
to do next?

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:38.250
Following the improper use of Item-001 leading
to the untimely death of a high ranking Foundation

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:44.480
Staff member, the weapon was deemed too dangerous
and containment procedures were implemented.

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:48.160
Due to the high amount of radiation they were
found to emit, the nine children were placed

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:53.290
into lead lined bags and buried under 50 meters
of concrete beneath the church of San Marcos

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.470
de la Vida Eterna.

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:59.920
Though all of the children continue to be
functionally braindead, they still display

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:05.450
signs of life despite their containment, and
by order of the Overseer Council, have been

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.740
classified as a Thaumiel entity.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:11.500
The smell of fire and oil fills the air.

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:16.540
The sound of gears grinding can be heard between
the explosions and shrieks of terror.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:21.290
A man runs out of his house, only to have
his leg grabbed by a metal arm and dragged

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.160
back through his front door.

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:29.540
SCP-001 leaves a trail of metal fragments
and mechanical parts on the ground in the

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:31.030
wake of its destruction.

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:37.290
Iron chains swing from its form, cast iron
gears whirl within it, a glowing light throbs

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:39.720
form the center of its body.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:44.360
SCP-001 is consuming everything in its path.

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:50.370
After incorporating the truck chassis into
its being, SCP-001 rolls in a lumbering fashion

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:51.850
to the next house.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:54.910
It rips the gutters from the side of the building.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.670
Residents who live in the area flee their
neighborhood.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:02.410
All the while hoping that the mechanical monstrosity
skips over their house so they have something

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:05.020
to return to if they make it out alive.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:09.640
A section of SCP-001’s undercarriage drops
away from the main body.

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:13.330
It rolls down the street consuming more and
more material.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:16.680
The new entity resembles a human spine and
rib cage.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:19.370
It topples over unable to support itself.

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:24.190
The rib like formations extend out to grab
anything and everything within reach.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:28.800
The newly incorporated material forms what
can only be described as a head.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:32.580
Light from within the eye sockets fixate on
nearby civilians.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:37.050
The metallic creature picks up the people
and places them inside its exposed, steel,

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:38.050
rib cage.

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:41.920
Then it turns and spots a woman helplessly
trying to crawl away.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:46.279
The creature reaches out with a spiked tentacle
and wraps it around the woman’s body.

00:15:46.279 --> 00:15:49.300
She is placed inside of the chest cavity.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:53.860
Moments later a severed hand falls out of
the entity and onto the ground.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:58.990
The mechanical monster continues to gather
bodies and materials, incorporating them into

00:15:58.990 --> 00:15:59.990
its frame.

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:02.900
A growth begins to slowly expand on its back.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:08.270
It becomes so massive that the creature falls
over and uses its limbs to scurry into a nearby

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:09.270
house.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:12.360
There is a sickening crunching sound as the
growth bursts.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:17.480
From within emerge three humanoid creatures
resembling the civilians that the entity had

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:18.750
consumed earlier.

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:23.410
A female with chains extending from her scalp
like dreadlocks stumbles away.

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:26.410
The second humanoid is a man with cogs for
limbs.

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:31.260
He examines the clock-like components that
have been incorporated into his body, then

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:33.320
stares blankly into the distance.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.820
The third humanoid lies motionless on the
ground.

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.620
He did not make it.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:40.980
The two functioning humanoids look at their
creator intently.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:45.860
For a moment nothing moves, then as if they
have been given orders telepathically, the

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:50.060
half human half machine humanoids turn and
run away from the mayhem.

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:56.000
A few weeks before the massacre caused by
what would be designated as SCP-001, the Foundation

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:58.170
had been in contact with the Allied Occult
Initiative.

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:02.980
There were rumors of an anomalous object in
Mexico being worshipped by a group of people

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:06.750
who identified themselves as The Church of
the Broken God.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:11.130
Intel about the Church claimed their deity
was a small mechanical box filled with cogs

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.320
and pistons.

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:16.950
The box supposedly had supernatural abilities,
it was said to be able to communicate with

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:20.260
congregants of The Church of the Broken God
telepathically.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:25.390
The devout worshiped the box, following any
order it gave, and in return they were filled

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:29.200
with an emotion that could only be described
as divine.

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:34.360
As World War II rages on in Europe, the Foundation
sends agents to recover anomalies in Mexico

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.100
that might help with the war effort.

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:39.770
While there, the Foundation force is tasked
with learning more about The Church of the

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:40.990
Broken God.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:44.970
They are also ordered to investigate a town
near La Paz where there are troubling accounts

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:48.070
of a mechanical anomalous creatures causing
mayhem.

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:52.690
The agents make their way through Mexico gathering
various objects to bring back to Foundation

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:54.800
sites in the United States.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:58.920
The unit loads all of the anomalies they’ve
recovered onto a train with the plan to check

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:03.220
out the stories of the mechanical anomaly
they’ve heard about as they make their way

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.220
to the U.S. border.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:07.420
The train heads north along rusted rails.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:11.690
Just outside of La Paz they come across a
broken down train filled with what looks to

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:12.690
be refugees.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:17.040
When the Foundation unit goes to investigate
they find all of the refugees repeating the

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:21.430
same words over and over again but they don’t
understand.

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:25.640
The Foundation agents look at one another
confused, until one of them translates the

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:27.340
words into English.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:32.200
The words the refugees are saying over and
over again are “la máquina, la máquina…

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.601
the machine, the machine,”

00:18:33.601 --> 00:18:38.410
The commanding officer orders a squad of Foundation
agents to proceed up the tracks, to see if

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:41.600
they can figure out what has the refugees
so scared.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:45.380
They make their way towards La Paz, disappearing
over the horizon.

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:49.490
As the sun sets the remaining Foundation agents
hear gunshots in the distance.

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:55.050
They stay awake all night remaining vigilant,
waiting for the exploratory squad, but morning

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:57.550
comes without anyone returning.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:01.620
Three days later, the Foundation force still
has not seen anything since the exploratory

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:02.630
squad left.

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:07.950
Then as the sun sits lazily in the morning
sky, a lone figure is spotted walking down

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.040
the tracks towards the trains.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:13.430
One of the agents on watch blows his whistle
and points to the figure.

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:16.450
A squad of agents rushes towards the shadow
of a man.

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.890
Their guns are raised, ready for anything.

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:22.750
The figure drops to the ground and begins
to crawl along the tracks.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:27.040
The agents reach the fallen man, only to find
that he is one of their squadmates who had

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:31.200
been sent up the tracks to investigate La
Paz several days before.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:32.890
The agent’s name is DeMarco.

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:34.040
He is covered in blood.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:37.260
His clothes are in tatters and he has lost
a boot.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:42.200
DeMarco lies on his back with Foundation agents
standing around him, his eyes are wide and

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.200
wild.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:47.540
He keeps babbling on about a “world eater,”
how the rest of his squad had been mulched,

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:50.110
and he is the only one who made it out alive.

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:54.610
The Foundation agents carry DeMarco back to
the makeshift base they created by the trains.

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:59.770
They need to figure out a way to get the convoy
moving again, but whatever is up ahead has

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:02.290
taken out an entire Foundation squad.

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:05.920
It had to be something anomalous, but what
could it possibly be?

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:09.280
The unit of Foundation agents prepare to move
towards La Paz.

00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:13.480
They start loading their rifles and check
the amount of ammunition and explosives available

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.630
in case the containment process gets out of
hand.

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:20.570
Just as they are about to leave the base,
a convoy appears on the horizon.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:25.000
It is an Allied Occult Initiative force preparing
to attack whatever it is that is devastating

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.140
La Paz.

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:31.340
This organization’s mission is not to secure,
contain, or protect, but to destroy.

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:35.380
The Foundation may be in over their heads
on this one, and the joint force with the

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:41.480
Allied Occult Initiative may be the only way
to stop what is now known as SCP-001.

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:44.620
The AOI and Foundation force gears up for
battle.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:49.750
They set out for La Paz, and what they find
causes them to quake with fear.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:54.920
SCP-001 has consumed so much material it is
the size of a mountain.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:21:00.450
It moves like a tidal wave of mechanical destruction,
washing over the buildings and landscape under

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:01.450
it.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:07.400
Whatever SCP-001 passes over is consumed and
added to its massive body.

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:13.380
SCP-001 started as a small mechanical box
with cogs, but now has morphed into a gigantic

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:15.190
metal death machine.

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:20.640
The Church of the Broken God has finally met
their maker, as the small entity they once

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:23.860
worshiped has now consumed all of its members.

00:21:23.860 --> 00:21:27.140
Their god is an all consuming monster.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:32.980
The AOI and Foundation forces do everything
they can to stop SCP-001 from continuing its

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:34.510
reign of destruction.

00:21:34.510 --> 00:21:39.000
They fire barrage after barrage of bullets
and explosives into the mechanical anomaly.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:43.870
They bring in air support to try and damage
it from the skies, but nothing works.

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:49.380
The AOI uses an artifact in their possession
to lure SCP-001 to the coast of the Pacific

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:53.090
Ocean where a trap has been set for the so-called
god.

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:56.520
The monstrous mechanical creature moves slowly
towards the water.

00:21:56.520 --> 00:22:00.920
It consumes abandoned cars, buildings, and
boats as it approaches the coastline.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:05.700
It even shovels large amounts of the earth
into its form, causing flames to spurt out

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:07.750
from its inner workings.

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:12.520
Smoke bellows from openings between different
mechanical components, like a volcano before

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:14.180
it is about to erupt.

00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:20.190
Suddenly, seemingly from nowhere, a massive
cloud with a reddish tint appears in the sky.

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:22.900
Air raid sirens can be heard in the distance.

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:25.170
The enormous cloud begins to pulsate.

00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:27.550
Streaks of lightning shoot through the red
mist in the sky.

00:22:27.550 --> 00:22:31.270
It now sits directly over SCP-001.

00:22:31.270 --> 00:22:33.820
From within the cloud part of a ship can be
seen.

00:22:33.820 --> 00:22:38.080
It appears to be slightly damaged, electricity
flows over its hull.

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:43.000
The vessel in the giant red cloud is classified
as SCP-2399.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:46.140
The underside of the vessel begins to glow
aqua blue.

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:51.970
A blinding beam of light is ejected from SCP-2399,
which penetrates straight down and through

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:54.850
SCP-001.

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:57.680
For a moment everything is still.

00:22:57.680 --> 00:22:59.610
There is complete silence.

00:22:59.610 --> 00:23:05.460
Then as if SCP-001 is trying to reach up and
grab the vessel above it, a mechanical bulge

00:23:05.460 --> 00:23:06.510
reaches out.

00:23:06.510 --> 00:23:12.510
Before SCP-001 can grab the vessel above,
there is another bright flash of light.

00:23:12.510 --> 00:23:15.330
SCP-2399 blinks out of existence.

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:19.250
The sound of grinding gears can be heard coming
from within SCP-001.

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:22.990
It begins to shed its outer layers of metal.

00:23:22.990 --> 00:23:29.300
Then the entire structure that was SCP-001
collapses into the water and onto the beach.

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:31.320
Giant cogs fall from the sky.

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.670
Parts of vehicles embed themselves in the
sand.

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:38.750
As the Foundation and AOI agents approach
the piles of scrap metal and mechanical components

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:41.270
they see that some of them are still moving.

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:46.020
It is as if an invisible powersource is still
pulsating through some of the machinery.

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:49.870
The agents of the Foundation celebrate the
destruction of the giant mechanical beast,

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:55.320
but little do they know this was only a piece
of the entity worshipped as the Broken God.

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:58.770
The Foundation agents collect as many of the
still moving parts as they can.

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:02.940
They find spinning gears, twitching pulleys,
and firing pistons.

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:06.370
As the parts are separated from one another
and carried away from the main wreckage of

00:24:06.370 --> 00:24:11.440
SCP-001, they slowly stop moving and become
inactive.

00:24:11.440 --> 00:24:15.320
Some of the artifacts recovered were identified
as being connected to the Church of the Broken

00:24:15.320 --> 00:24:16.320
God.

00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:22.490
These artifacts are found closer to the middle
of what was once a mountain sized SCP-001.

00:24:22.490 --> 00:24:27.600
Hundreds of anomalous artifacts are collected
and transported to SCP Foundation sites.

00:24:27.600 --> 00:24:31.510
Collecting the broken parts of SCP-001 is
relatively safe.

00:24:31.510 --> 00:24:35.630
However, some agents get too close to the
larger moving parts, getting caught in them

00:24:35.630 --> 00:24:37.350
and losing a body part or two.

00:24:37.350 --> 00:24:41.970
But most agents proceed with caution and survive
the collection ordeal with their arms and

00:24:41.970 --> 00:24:44.470
legs still attached to their bodies.

00:24:44.470 --> 00:24:48.240
Dive teams are sent into the water to recover
parts that have sunk to the bottom of the

00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:49.240
sea.

00:24:49.240 --> 00:24:51.160
One of the divers is a local from the area.

00:24:51.160 --> 00:24:55.650
He is hired to bring up the heart of the machine,
since he is an experienced diver used to free

00:24:55.650 --> 00:24:59.749
diving to great depths to collect oysters
from the bottom of the bay.

00:24:59.749 --> 00:25:03.040
The diver enters the water and swims down
into the murky depths.

00:25:03.040 --> 00:25:08.720
He secures straps around the heart of SCP-001
and pulls hard on the rope, as an indication

00:25:08.720 --> 00:25:11.350
to the surface that it is ready to be hauled
up.

00:25:11.350 --> 00:25:13.890
The salvage team on the surface begins to
pull.

00:25:13.890 --> 00:25:17.180
There is a second slight tug on the rope,
then it goes slack.

00:25:17.180 --> 00:25:18.930
The team continues to pull.

00:25:18.930 --> 00:25:24.090
When they get the heart to the surface they
are horrified at what else comes up with it.

00:25:24.090 --> 00:25:27.520
Tangled in the ropes is the lifeless body
of the diver.

00:25:27.520 --> 00:25:31.400
His head is smashed between two moving pieces
of the heart.

00:25:31.400 --> 00:25:36.050
It looks as if he shoved his head between
the slabs of metal himself.

00:25:36.050 --> 00:25:41.190
The salvage team untangles the body, rolls
it off the deck, and back into the ocean.

00:25:41.190 --> 00:25:46.530
The mechanical box which was the heart of
SCP-001 is offloaded onto the shore, but as

00:25:46.530 --> 00:25:51.320
the Foundation prepares to move it to a containment
facility, the weather starts to deteriorate.

00:25:51.320 --> 00:25:54.940
Hurricane force winds sweep across the water
and batter the coast.

00:25:54.940 --> 00:25:58.430
The heart is kept in a secured storage warehouse
until it can be moved.

00:25:58.430 --> 00:26:02.800
The people living in the village nearby complain
of hearing voices and rashes so itchy that

00:26:02.800 --> 00:26:05.350
they practically tear their skin off.

00:26:05.350 --> 00:26:09.290
Once the storm passes, the Foundation agents
load the heart onto a ship.

00:26:09.290 --> 00:26:12.870
It is to be transported to a Foundation site
just across the border.

00:26:12.870 --> 00:26:15.220
The ocean seems calm and serene.

00:26:15.220 --> 00:26:18.760
The Foundation ship undocks and begins its
journey up the coast.

00:26:18.760 --> 00:26:22.809
Not too long after beginning its journey the
ship slowly drifts off course.

00:26:22.809 --> 00:26:27.410
It is as if the crew has stopped manning their
posts, and the ship is being controlled by

00:26:27.410 --> 00:26:28.900
a mind of its own.

00:26:28.900 --> 00:26:34.030
The Foundation ship crashes and sinks somewhere
in the Pacific Ocean, never to be found, and

00:26:34.030 --> 00:26:40.100
more importantly, the heart of SCP-001 doesn’t
make it to the Foundation site.

00:26:40.100 --> 00:26:42.690
Years later a man is walking along the beach.

00:26:42.690 --> 00:26:43.830
He hears something.

00:26:43.830 --> 00:26:48.110
It sounds like someone pounding on a large
drum to the rhythm of a heartbeat.

00:26:48.110 --> 00:26:50.370
The man walks towards the sound.

00:26:50.370 --> 00:26:54.250
Something is drawing him forward, closer and
closer to the heartbeat.

00:26:54.250 --> 00:26:57.260
He walks and walks until the beating stops.

00:26:57.260 --> 00:26:59.860
He bends down and moves the sand aside.

00:26:59.860 --> 00:27:03.730
He spots the corner of a mechanical box sticking
out of the white sand.

00:27:03.730 --> 00:27:07.330
The man digs deeper and pulls out the small
box.

00:27:07.330 --> 00:27:10.590
Inside he can see gears whirling and pistons
firing.

00:27:10.590 --> 00:27:13.110
He holds the box close to his own heart.

00:27:13.110 --> 00:27:15.360
It seems to speak to him.

00:27:15.360 --> 00:27:17.700
The man brings the box back to town.

00:27:17.700 --> 00:27:22.540
He starts to worship the box and soon more
and more people in the area join the new religion.

00:27:22.540 --> 00:27:27.020
They cast aside their old beliefs and focus
on the powerful entity contained within the

00:27:27.020 --> 00:27:28.020
box.

00:27:28.020 --> 00:27:34.300
God is not dead… at least not yet, but the
prophecies of The Church of the Broken God

00:27:34.300 --> 00:27:40.220
say that when the heart is found, the God
will reassemble itself once again.

00:27:40.220 --> 00:27:46.710
Then the Unbroken God will destroy all other
false deities, until only he remains.

00:27:46.710 --> 00:27:52.580
It’s a quiet evening at Area-11 where the
Pietrykau-Fontaine Spatial Stabilization Array

00:27:52.580 --> 00:27:53.580
is housed.

00:27:53.580 --> 00:27:59.510
A skeleton crew is working overnight, to ensure
the array is ready for its big test the following

00:27:59.510 --> 00:28:00.510
day.

00:28:00.510 --> 00:28:04.260
The Foundation has been working on a particle
accelerator that will contain anomalies with

00:28:04.260 --> 00:28:07.530
the ability to manipulate the nature of spacetime.

00:28:07.530 --> 00:28:12.220
The preliminary tests seem promising, but
a few last minute tweaks to the array are

00:28:12.220 --> 00:28:13.309
necessary.

00:28:13.309 --> 00:28:19.150
Unfortunately, it is on this night in 1982,
that marks the beginning of the end for the

00:28:19.150 --> 00:28:20.860
SCP Foundation.

00:28:20.860 --> 00:28:25.720
Dr. Calvin Desmet is monitoring the array
and he notices as it spools up that there

00:28:25.720 --> 00:28:29.559
are some minor power fluctuations in one of
the stabilization arms.

00:28:29.559 --> 00:28:33.880
This problem is not uncommon due to the vast
amounts of energy being pumped through the

00:28:33.880 --> 00:28:38.870
array and the harmonic resonance the machine
gives off, which slowly causes the coupling

00:28:38.870 --> 00:28:40.440
rings to loosen.

00:28:40.440 --> 00:28:45.570
Calvin Desmet decides that remounting the
stabilization rings will be an easy fix.

00:28:45.570 --> 00:28:47.170
And it’s a necessary one.

00:28:47.170 --> 00:28:52.350
He knows that if the rings fail during the
actual test, the array could end up shut down

00:28:52.350 --> 00:28:53.440
for months.

00:28:53.440 --> 00:28:58.050
There is still plenty of time, so Calvin Desmet
grabs his toolbox and heads down into the

00:28:58.050 --> 00:28:59.050
array.

00:28:59.050 --> 00:29:03.150
The machine is still spooling, keeping the
energy flowing at a constant low rate.

00:29:03.150 --> 00:29:07.690
There is no danger at the moment, as the inside
of the array is shielded from the radiation

00:29:07.690 --> 00:29:10.059
and energy pulsing through the outer ring.

00:29:10.059 --> 00:29:12.860
But then something unexpected happens.

00:29:12.860 --> 00:29:16.740
The system’s primary generator begins to
fluctuate uncontrollably.

00:29:16.740 --> 00:29:19.230
A catastrophic failure is imminent.

00:29:19.230 --> 00:29:24.670
Sirens begin to sound, the facility is evacuated
and the chamber is sealed.

00:29:24.670 --> 00:29:29.190
Deep in the bowels of the array Calvin Desmet
cannot hear the evacuation announcement.

00:29:29.190 --> 00:29:34.070
The humming of the array echoes through the
chamber, dampening all sound from the outside

00:29:34.070 --> 00:29:35.070
world.

00:29:35.070 --> 00:29:38.610
The array begins to come online while Desmet
continues to work on the coupling.

00:29:38.610 --> 00:29:42.110
He has no idea what is about to happen.

00:29:42.110 --> 00:29:45.950
Meanwhile a team of Foundation scientists
scramble to get the power fluctuations in

00:29:45.950 --> 00:29:47.980
the main generator under control.

00:29:47.980 --> 00:29:51.000
As they frantically work, catastrophe strikes.

00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:55.210
They initiate the power-down cycle, but as
the generator struggles to keep the power

00:29:55.210 --> 00:29:58.450
flow balanced, an energy surge builds up.

00:29:58.450 --> 00:30:04.170
A massive amount of energy is released all
at once causing the main reactor to explode.

00:30:04.170 --> 00:30:08.610
The entire structure rocks back and forth
and Desmet is thrown into the side of the

00:30:08.610 --> 00:30:09.610
array.

00:30:09.610 --> 00:30:13.660
He too now knows that something is very wrong
and runs for the exit.

00:30:13.660 --> 00:30:16.380
When he reaches the door he finds it has been
sealed.

00:30:16.380 --> 00:30:20.690
In a panic Desmet continues running through
the tube to the next access point.

00:30:20.690 --> 00:30:22.500
This door has been locked as well.

00:30:22.500 --> 00:30:27.880
He’s never been so scared in his entire
life, and he shakes uncontrollably from the

00:30:27.880 --> 00:30:30.250
adrenaline being dumped into his muscles.

00:30:30.250 --> 00:30:33.670
The surge of energy rushes through the array
towards Desmet.

00:30:33.670 --> 00:30:37.230
A singularity begins to form in the containment
chamber.

00:30:37.230 --> 00:30:41.559
The array is working just as it should, except
that there was never supposed to be a person

00:30:41.559 --> 00:30:45.820
inside as the singularity was brought into
existence.

00:30:45.820 --> 00:30:50.240
Moments after the singularity forms, the massive
pull of its gravity causes the stabilizer

00:30:50.240 --> 00:30:53.030
arm that Desmet had been working on to fail.

00:30:53.030 --> 00:30:59.940
The side of the array is ripped off, and Calvin
Desmet stares into the naked eye of the singularity.

00:30:59.940 --> 00:31:05.800
Everything is silent and still for a moment,
then the singularity collapses in on itself,

00:31:05.800 --> 00:31:11.590
taking the test chamber and much of the research
wing with it along with Dr. Calvin Desmet.

00:31:11.590 --> 00:31:16.120
Sparking wires hang from the exposed walls
and ceiling where the singularity ripped the

00:31:16.120 --> 00:31:17.990
main structure away.

00:31:17.990 --> 00:31:22.070
Water flows into the deep hole carved out
of the earth where the array once stood.

00:31:22.070 --> 00:31:26.570
The scientists from Area-11 look into the
crater left by the collapsed singularity.

00:31:26.570 --> 00:31:31.120
The Foundation administration sends agents
to collect the staff at the site and document

00:31:31.120 --> 00:31:32.990
the failings of the project.

00:31:32.990 --> 00:31:36.010
They conclude that the accident was caused
by human error.

00:31:36.010 --> 00:31:41.080
They order the array to be rebuilt, this time
using entirely automated systems to eliminate

00:31:41.080 --> 00:31:43.920
the chances of another mishap occurring.

00:31:43.920 --> 00:31:48.620
Several years after the catastrophic event
at Area-11 a new array is constructed.

00:31:48.620 --> 00:31:53.520
An intelligence system called NETZACH is put
in charge of overseeing its functions.

00:31:53.520 --> 00:31:57.880
It is a super computer that is programmed
to follow commands, but can also autonomously

00:31:57.880 --> 00:32:01.900
make decisions in order to prevent any failures
in the system.

00:32:01.900 --> 00:32:04.690
Experiments begin again in May of 2006.

00:32:04.690 --> 00:32:10.040
The new array soon manifests its first singularity
in the containment chamber at Area-11 and

00:32:10.040 --> 00:32:15.700
what happens next will forever change the
Foundation… and the multiverse.

00:32:15.700 --> 00:32:20.179
The singularity is kept stable in the array,
it seems as if the Foundation has succeeded

00:32:20.179 --> 00:32:23.000
in trapping and containing spatial anomalies.

00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:28.080
But as they run more diagnostics on the anomaly,
something unexpected happens.

00:32:28.080 --> 00:32:31.210
The singularity begins to grow in size.

00:32:31.210 --> 00:32:35.070
The point of infinite gravity threatens to
breach containment as it reaches the boundaries

00:32:35.070 --> 00:32:36.380
of the array.

00:32:36.380 --> 00:32:40.900
Just before contact, the singularity’s growth
slows, and then stops.

00:32:40.900 --> 00:32:46.750
NETZACH has made the split second calculations
and adjustments necessary to contain the singularity.

00:32:46.750 --> 00:32:51.760
The artificial intelligence has saved the
facility and the lives of everyone in it.

00:32:51.760 --> 00:32:57.600
Now, sitting in the array, is a thick rotating
cloud of radioactive gas and dust, obscuring

00:32:57.600 --> 00:32:59.710
the singularity within.

00:32:59.710 --> 00:33:04.559
As Foundation scientists work rapidly to fix
the array, odd events begin to occur.

00:33:04.559 --> 00:33:07.870
The workers hear noises that sound like painful
wailing.

00:33:07.870 --> 00:33:12.480
Over time the noises evolve into words, and
then full sentences.

00:33:12.480 --> 00:33:15.530
They seem to be originating from the singularity.

00:33:15.530 --> 00:33:20.300
Using equipment able to penetrate the thick
cloud of radioactive gas, the Foundation scientists

00:33:20.300 --> 00:33:22.410
get a glimpse at the singularity.

00:33:22.410 --> 00:33:27.490
To their surprise, the singularity has taken
on the shape of a human.

00:33:27.490 --> 00:33:31.100
The scientists work frantically to figure
out how the singularity could have formed

00:33:31.100 --> 00:33:32.809
itself into a humanoid shape.

00:33:32.809 --> 00:33:37.660
Dr. J. Barton Ramsey is the first to try and
make contact with the humanoid within the

00:33:37.660 --> 00:33:38.660
singularity.

00:33:38.660 --> 00:33:42.100
He finds that the entity cannot communicate
in the traditional sense.

00:33:42.100 --> 00:33:48.280
The massive gravitational pull of the singularity
does not allow sound to escape its void, instead,

00:33:48.280 --> 00:33:53.740
the entity manipulates gravity to vibrate
the suspension rings of the array itself and

00:33:53.740 --> 00:33:55.730
create soundwaves.

00:33:55.730 --> 00:34:00.490
The being in the singularity whispers in a
metallic voice created by the vibrating of

00:34:00.490 --> 00:34:04.420
the array’s rings and says “Johannes Ramsey.”

00:34:04.420 --> 00:34:07.450
Dr. Ramsey steps back from the observation
window.

00:34:07.450 --> 00:34:10.140
“How do you know my name?” he asks the
entity.

00:34:10.140 --> 00:34:14.270
The humanoid within the swirling gas cloud
identifies itself as having the memories of

00:34:14.270 --> 00:34:15.600
Calvin Desmet.

00:34:15.600 --> 00:34:21.050
It is not Desmet per se, the being in the
singularity is so much more than one person,

00:34:21.050 --> 00:34:26.240
but it was somehow created by the accident
that had sucked Calvin Desmet into the singularity

00:34:26.240 --> 00:34:27.280
years before.

00:34:27.280 --> 00:34:32.760
The entity seems to switch between the mind
of Desmet and the vast infinity of the cosmos.

00:34:32.760 --> 00:34:36.960
The Desmet entity asks for an Overseer from
the Foundation to be brought in.

00:34:36.960 --> 00:34:39.950
It has a proposal for the O-5 Council.

00:34:39.950 --> 00:34:44.570
When Dr. Ramsey asks why the entity needs
to talk to the The Overseers it replies that

00:34:44.570 --> 00:34:49.250
it wants “to offer them a way out.”

00:34:49.250 --> 00:34:54.190
The following day, O5-1 enters the facility
and heads to the observation deck.

00:34:54.190 --> 00:34:58.910
He looks through the reinforced glass at the
swirling cloud of radioactive dust, then glances

00:34:58.910 --> 00:35:02.520
at a monitor to see the humanoid shape of
the singularity within.

00:35:02.520 --> 00:35:06.400
He presses the microphone button on the console
and addresses the entity.

00:35:06.400 --> 00:35:09.009
“To whom am I speaking?” he asks.

00:35:09.009 --> 00:35:14.810
For simplicity sake the entity tells O5-1
to refer to him as Calvin Desmet.

00:35:14.810 --> 00:35:20.440
O5-1 makes notes of the events unfolding before
him and then asks about the way out that Calvin

00:35:20.440 --> 00:35:21.440
had mentioned.

00:35:21.440 --> 00:35:23.760
The air is still for a moment.

00:35:23.760 --> 00:35:28.710
Then Desmet begins to speak through the vibrations
of the structure once again.

00:35:28.710 --> 00:35:34.400
He informs O5-1 that what the SCP Foundation
is doing by securing and containing anomalous

00:35:34.400 --> 00:35:39.820
entities around the world, is like putting
a small Band-Aid on a much bigger wound.

00:35:39.820 --> 00:35:44.930
Desmet wants to propose a final solution to
all of the Foundation’s problems.

00:35:44.930 --> 00:35:50.400
O5-1 listens intently as the entity unravels
the mysteries of where the SCPs have come

00:35:50.400 --> 00:35:51.400
from.

00:35:51.400 --> 00:35:55.990
He explains that the anomalies that the Foundation
has worked so hard to secure, contain, and

00:35:55.990 --> 00:36:01.730
protect the human race from are actually bleeding
into their reality from a vast multiverse.

00:36:01.730 --> 00:36:06.940
The only way to stop the manifestation of
anomalies into this universe… is to destroy

00:36:06.940 --> 00:36:08.810
all other realities.

00:36:08.810 --> 00:36:14.810
The entity that is Calvin Desmet tells O5-1
that he is able to bring about this destruction…

00:36:14.810 --> 00:36:18.530
if they release him from the confines of the
array.

00:36:18.530 --> 00:36:24.369
O5-1 is transfixed by the swirling gas that
is promising him, and everyone else on Earth,

00:36:24.369 --> 00:36:25.369
salvation.

00:36:25.369 --> 00:36:27.440
He shakes his head in disbelief.

00:36:27.440 --> 00:36:28.990
Could this be true?

00:36:28.990 --> 00:36:34.000
O5-1 turns away from the swirling gas and
begins to walk away from the viewing glass.

00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:36.470
“I’ll need to think about what you’re
saying.”

00:36:36.470 --> 00:36:38.830
The structure begins to shake slightly.

00:36:38.830 --> 00:36:43.300
The voice of Calvin Desmet reverberates off
of the array a little louder than before.

00:36:43.300 --> 00:36:49.770
“Choose quickly Overseer, although it won’t
happen for decades, eventually a catastrophic

00:36:49.770 --> 00:36:53.250
SCP event will wipe out life on this planet.

00:36:53.250 --> 00:36:59.050
Perhaps not in your lifetime… but it will
most certainly happen within the lifetime

00:36:59.050 --> 00:37:01.170
of your children.

00:37:01.170 --> 00:37:04.310
We will talk again soon.”

00:37:04.310 --> 00:37:07.390
The vibrations slow and then stop completely.

00:37:07.390 --> 00:37:12.020
There is an eerie stillness in the observation
room as O5-1 walks out.

00:37:12.020 --> 00:37:16.600
The next day all staff members located at
Area-11 are relocated to other Foundation

00:37:16.600 --> 00:37:18.640
sites and given amnestics.

00:37:18.640 --> 00:37:24.590
The O5 Council meets in a large circular room
with wood paneling and no windows.

00:37:24.590 --> 00:37:29.160
O5-1 begins the meeting by telling the others
what Calvin Desmet had described about the

00:37:29.160 --> 00:37:30.510
end of the world.

00:37:30.510 --> 00:37:34.560
He pauses for what seems like an eternity
and then tells them of Desmet’s offer that

00:37:34.560 --> 00:37:39.480
he could prevent the end of the world, but
at the cost of destroying an infinite number

00:37:39.480 --> 00:37:41.070
of other realities.

00:37:41.070 --> 00:37:46.790
This would mean that all the humans and creatures
of those realities would be destroyed as well.

00:37:46.790 --> 00:37:50.830
Was murdering countless other beings worth
it to protect their own reality?

00:37:50.830 --> 00:37:56.100
O5-1 begins to shake, he hasn't slept or eaten
anything since his talk with Desmet.

00:37:56.100 --> 00:37:59.230
He's being torn apart from the inside.

00:37:59.230 --> 00:38:02.369
O5-3 stands up and addresses the council.

00:38:02.369 --> 00:38:06.770
He informs everyone in the room that independent
teams have conducted research into what the

00:38:06.770 --> 00:38:11.300
Calvin Desmet entity has claimed… and they
found it to be true.

00:38:11.300 --> 00:38:14.190
The world really would come to an end.

00:38:14.190 --> 00:38:18.630
Furthermore, the research teams determined
that the capabilities of Desmet would in fact

00:38:18.630 --> 00:38:21.470
allow him to dismantle the other realities.

00:38:21.470 --> 00:38:26.840
O5-3 insists that the council must vote to
allow Desmet to destroy the other realities

00:38:26.840 --> 00:38:29.990
to ensure that this reality could be saved.

00:38:29.990 --> 00:38:33.710
They must strike now, before the world is
overrun.

00:38:33.710 --> 00:38:39.800
O5-1 continues to shake while O5-3 breathes
heavily, sweat pouring down his temples.

00:38:39.800 --> 00:38:43.030
The rest of the council shifts their gazes
from side to side.

00:38:43.030 --> 00:38:45.410
It is time for a vote.

00:38:45.410 --> 00:38:50.320
There are eight “ayes” to allow Desmet
to destroy all other realities and four “nays”

00:38:50.320 --> 00:38:51.730
against the plan.

00:38:51.730 --> 00:38:56.970
O5-3 stands and walks around the room, stopping
behind each “nay” voter and putting a

00:38:56.970 --> 00:38:58.590
bullet in their head.

00:38:58.590 --> 00:39:05.400
He stops at the last, O5-9, who pulls out
a gun, places it under her own chin, and pulls

00:39:05.400 --> 00:39:06.640
the trigger.

00:39:06.640 --> 00:39:09.820
O5-13 abstains from the vote and the measure
passes.

00:39:09.820 --> 00:39:14.610
The remaining Overseers will use the Calvin
Desmet entity to save their reality at the

00:39:14.610 --> 00:39:20.290
expense of all others, and they soon head
to Area-11 to execute their plan.

00:39:20.290 --> 00:39:26.260
O5-1, 4, and 12 enter the observation room
that looks upon the swirling radioactive gas

00:39:26.260 --> 00:39:27.980
around Calvin Desmet.

00:39:27.980 --> 00:39:32.550
O5-1 orders NETZACH to begin powering down
the array, which will allow the entity to

00:39:32.550 --> 00:39:35.200
prove he can do what he has promised.

00:39:35.200 --> 00:39:40.540
They have pinpointed the reality that SCP-884
came from and the shaving mirror itself sits

00:39:40.540 --> 00:39:43.390
on a table in another room in the facility.

00:39:43.390 --> 00:39:48.369
O5-3 stands in the room, watching the mirror
to see if anything happens.

00:39:48.369 --> 00:39:52.870
O5-1 asks Calvin Desmet to eliminate the reality
that the mirror had come from.

00:39:52.870 --> 00:39:57.369
The room shakes as the entity uses it to acknowledge
the request.

00:39:57.369 --> 00:40:03.349
Moments later the phone rings in the observation
room, it is O5-3, he informs the others that

00:40:03.349 --> 00:40:05.170
the mirror has disappeared.

00:40:05.170 --> 00:40:10.590
Its reality has been destroyed, and therefore
it no longer exists.

00:40:10.590 --> 00:40:15.810
There is a sigh of relief in the room as the
Overseers realize that this just might work.

00:40:15.810 --> 00:40:21.640
O5-1 asks Calvin Desmet to continue and destroy
all the realities that are bleeding into their

00:40:21.640 --> 00:40:22.640
own.

00:40:22.640 --> 00:40:25.840
This time the entire facility begins to quake.

00:40:25.840 --> 00:40:31.200
Suddenly, O5-1 jerks backwards, his eyes wide
in confusion and horror.

00:40:31.200 --> 00:40:34.630
His body seems to be compressing under an
unknown force.

00:40:34.630 --> 00:40:39.960
O5-1 begins to distort, his legs and arms
fold into the core of his body.

00:40:39.960 --> 00:40:45.900
His head snaps down, and all that was O5-1
is sucked down into a single point in space

00:40:45.900 --> 00:40:48.160
before it completely disappears.

00:40:48.160 --> 00:40:52.410
Calvin Desmet then turns his attention to
the other two Overseers in the room who both

00:40:52.410 --> 00:40:57.170
seem to collapse into blackholes of their
own in the center of their bodies.

00:40:57.170 --> 00:41:01.430
NETZACH's warning klaxon begins to sound,
signalling that the emergency failsafe has

00:41:01.430 --> 00:41:02.670
been activated.

00:41:02.670 --> 00:41:06.810
Before Calvin Desmet is brought under control,
the structural supports in the entire facility

00:41:06.810 --> 00:41:08.700
vibrate with his words.

00:41:08.700 --> 00:41:12.610
They are in a voice that sounds strangely
similar to O5-1’s.

00:41:12.610 --> 00:41:17.490
“Your children are free to live lives that
do not end in horror.

00:41:17.490 --> 00:41:20.070
An end to your perpetual struggle.

00:41:20.070 --> 00:41:22.580
An end to darkness.

00:41:22.580 --> 00:41:26.170
The freedom to live in the light.

00:41:26.170 --> 00:41:29.780
All traces must be removed.

00:41:29.780 --> 00:41:32.580
This world must be washed clean.

00:41:32.580 --> 00:41:35.960
The Foundation does not escape atonement.

00:41:35.960 --> 00:41:38.520
It is the only way out.”

00:41:38.520 --> 00:41:40.619
It had been a deception.

00:41:40.619 --> 00:41:46.180
The Calvin Desmet entity had no intention
of stopping anomalies from infiltrating this

00:41:46.180 --> 00:41:52.000
world, it wanted to remove all traces of the
anomalous from all universes including this

00:41:52.000 --> 00:41:56.160
one, and that meant destroying the Overseers
and the Foundation itself.

00:41:56.160 --> 00:42:00.840
Their destruction would serve as an atonement
for the pain and suffering they had caused

00:42:00.840 --> 00:42:04.700
in their quest to secure and contain the anomalous.

00:42:04.700 --> 00:42:09.470
Calvin had to lie to the Overseers about the
real plan, since he knew they’d never sacrifice

00:42:09.470 --> 00:42:15.180
themselves and the foundation, even if it
meant an end to anomalies plaguing our world.

00:42:15.180 --> 00:42:19.940
Now though, with the Overseers out of the
way, the Calvin Desmet entity is free to move

00:42:19.940 --> 00:42:24.640
forward with its plan and purge all realities
of any trace of the anomalous.

00:42:24.640 --> 00:42:30.080
But just then NETZACH’s failsafes kick in
and the Pietrykau-Fontaine Spatial Stabilization

00:42:30.080 --> 00:42:33.290
Array subdues the entity's abilities.

00:42:33.290 --> 00:42:35.470
Desmet is once again contained.

00:42:35.470 --> 00:42:39.740
O5-3 bursts through the door and into the
observation room.

00:42:39.740 --> 00:42:44.070
He stands before the shattered glass of the
window that looks into the array.

00:42:44.070 --> 00:42:48.680
O5-3 asks NETZACH how long the containment
array can hold Calvin Desmet.

00:42:48.680 --> 00:42:54.750
The computer’s voice fades in and out but
says, “Given current conditions, one-hundred

00:42:54.750 --> 00:42:59.670
and nineteen days, six hours, and forty-seven
minutes.”

00:42:59.670 --> 00:43:05.770
O5-3 sighs, he tells NETZACH to make a note
in the SCP database that the Calvin Desmet

00:43:05.770 --> 00:43:07.850
entity will now be known as SCP-001.

00:43:07.850 --> 00:43:16.430
Then to make dozens of other randomly generated
entries and label them as SCP-001 as well.

00:43:16.430 --> 00:43:22.080
He knows that they will need to keep the true
nature of what this entity can do a secret.

00:43:22.080 --> 00:43:24.050
O5-3 walks out of the room.

00:43:24.050 --> 00:43:28.680
Under his breath he speaks to himself, “they
said that I'll know the one true God when

00:43:28.680 --> 00:43:33.380
I see it, and to give that God everything
it wants, because that's the only thing that

00:43:33.380 --> 00:43:34.380
matters.

00:43:34.380 --> 00:43:38.090
Tonight it appears God wants to talk to me.”

00:43:38.090 --> 00:43:43.099
Calvin Lucien stands at the end of a dusty
table in an abandoned warehouse.

00:43:43.099 --> 00:43:46.620
In the shadows across from him sit several
hidden figures.

00:43:46.620 --> 00:43:51.050
The warehouse is falling apart, but is suitable
for the meeting Calvin has requested with

00:43:51.050 --> 00:43:53.060
the heads of the Chaos Insurgency.

00:43:53.060 --> 00:43:58.640
He has completed numerous missions for the
organization and each one has been successful;

00:43:58.640 --> 00:44:01.620
now he is proposing one final mission.

00:44:01.620 --> 00:44:05.930
Calvin Lucien takes a tattered journal out
of his bag and slides it across the table

00:44:05.930 --> 00:44:07.960
to the figures sitting in the shadows.

00:44:07.960 --> 00:44:12.650
“It’s a journal with details on the habits
of each of the thirteen Foundation Overseers,”

00:44:12.650 --> 00:44:14.090
he says.

00:44:14.090 --> 00:44:16.440
There is silence from the other end of the
table.

00:44:16.440 --> 00:44:20.420
A hand reaches out and grabs the journal;
the pages begin to turn.

00:44:20.420 --> 00:44:25.220
“The new models indicate an anomalous catastrophe
is imminent, not even the Foundation can stop

00:44:25.220 --> 00:44:26.220
it.

00:44:26.220 --> 00:44:29.810
The only way to save the world is to kill
the Overseers,” There are whispers from

00:44:29.810 --> 00:44:31.830
across the table as Calvin continues.

00:44:31.830 --> 00:44:35.400
“The proliferation of anomalies in the world
are the fault of the Overseers.

00:44:35.400 --> 00:44:40.260
They have been meddling with reality, if business
continues as usual we might not make it out

00:44:40.260 --> 00:44:41.530
of the 2020s.

00:44:41.530 --> 00:44:43.600
We need to act now.”

00:44:43.600 --> 00:44:49.670
The whispering from the shadows resumes, this
time with what seems to be a little more urgency.

00:44:49.670 --> 00:44:54.690
One of the voices asks the question on everyone’s
mind, “How do you plan to kill the Overseers?

00:44:54.690 --> 00:44:58.290
They have a deal with death, they are immortal.”

00:44:58.290 --> 00:45:01.740
Calvin smiles and takes out a small vial from
his jacket pocket.

00:45:01.740 --> 00:45:03.630
“With this,” he says.

00:45:03.630 --> 00:45:08.150
There is silence from the shadows.The journal
slides back across the table and comes to

00:45:08.150 --> 00:45:10.090
a stop right in front of Calvin.

00:45:10.090 --> 00:45:13.840
A deep voice from the shadows says, “do
it.”

00:45:13.840 --> 00:45:18.300
Calvin Lucien gathers his team; the codename
given to the group is “Killsquad.”

00:45:18.300 --> 00:45:21.710
He informs them they have been cleared to
take out the Overseers.

00:45:21.710 --> 00:45:26.730
It will be the most dangerous mission they’ve
ever been on, and even if successful, they

00:45:26.730 --> 00:45:28.130
probably won't make it out alive.

00:45:28.130 --> 00:45:32.980
But, the team is loyal, they set out to confront
the Thirteenth Overseer.

00:45:32.980 --> 00:45:39.040
This has to be their first stop because without
eliminating O5-13, nothing else will matter.

00:45:39.040 --> 00:45:44.210
It is this Overseer who has a deal with Death;
a deal that protects all of the Foundation

00:45:44.210 --> 00:45:45.980
Overseers from dying.

00:45:45.980 --> 00:45:49.180
If that deal can be broken, and O5-13 can
be eliminated, then Calvin Lucien and his

00:45:49.180 --> 00:45:52.910
team will have a shot at eradicating the other
Overseers.

00:45:52.910 --> 00:45:57.060
If the deal with Death cannot be broken, all
is lost.

00:45:57.060 --> 00:46:01.760
The team boards a ship at the tip of South
America and sails towards the frozen waters

00:46:01.760 --> 00:46:02.950
of Antarctica.

00:46:02.950 --> 00:46:05.880
The Killsquad is made up of Calvin and three
others.

00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:08.600
They sit in the galley preparing for the mission
ahead.

00:46:08.600 --> 00:46:12.910
Anthony Wright is a battle hardened soldier
who sits at one end of the table.

00:46:12.910 --> 00:46:15.099
His face is covered with scars.

00:46:15.099 --> 00:46:20.800
No one can remember when he first joined the
Insurgency because it was so long ago.

00:46:20.800 --> 00:46:22.780
Next to him is Olivia Torres.

00:46:22.780 --> 00:46:26.820
She is an anarchist who was recruited into
the Insurgency after she was liberated from

00:46:26.820 --> 00:46:29.120
a Foundation site during a raid.

00:46:29.120 --> 00:46:33.790
Adam Ivanov sits staring into his computer
screen, he is testing different gadgets that

00:46:33.790 --> 00:46:35.790
might be of use on the mission.

00:46:35.790 --> 00:46:39.550
He pushes his glasses up the bridge of his
nose and strikes the “enter” key.

00:46:39.550 --> 00:46:43.560
A long line of code begins to scroll across
the screen.

00:46:43.560 --> 00:46:48.080
A siren begins to sound, informing the crew
to make their way to the main deck.

00:46:48.080 --> 00:46:52.190
When they surface from the bowels of the ship
they see something in the distance.

00:46:52.190 --> 00:46:57.580
It is a giant black tower rising from the
depths of the ocean like an evil iceberg.

00:46:57.580 --> 00:47:02.930
Waves crash over the side of the railings,
drenching the deck and crew with frigid water.

00:47:02.930 --> 00:47:06.109
Calvin looks at the jagged rocks along the
shore of the tower.

00:47:06.109 --> 00:47:10.349
There is no way to safely dock; there is only
one way onto the island.

00:47:10.349 --> 00:47:13.150
They know what needs to be done.

00:47:13.150 --> 00:47:16.960
Anthony waits for the next wave, then opens
the throttle to full.

00:47:16.960 --> 00:47:19.820
The ship is carried toward the island on the
crest of the wave.

00:47:19.820 --> 00:47:23.930
The hull is impaled on the rocks surrounding
the tower sending everything flying towards

00:47:23.930 --> 00:47:25.040
the front of the boat.

00:47:25.040 --> 00:47:30.000
“See, that wasn’t so bad,” Calvin says
to his team as he bandages a gash on his head.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:34.190
Knowing what lays ahead Calvin orders his
team to wait on the ship while he makes his

00:47:34.190 --> 00:47:35.690
own deal with death.

00:47:35.690 --> 00:47:39.050
He enters the dark structure and is greeted
by a corpse.

00:47:39.050 --> 00:47:44.339
The corpse speaks to him, ejecting dust from
its lungs with every word; its breath smells

00:47:44.339 --> 00:47:46.130
like decaying flesh.

00:47:46.130 --> 00:47:50.820
Death has inhabited the body of Dr. Felix
Carter, the Thirteenth Overseer.

00:47:50.820 --> 00:47:54.840
Calvin is prepared though thanks to the notes
in the journal he possesses.

00:47:54.840 --> 00:47:59.410
Without hesitating, he takes out a small bottle
of liquid from his pocket and lunges at the

00:47:59.410 --> 00:48:00.410
corpse.

00:48:00.410 --> 00:48:04.650
He grabs it by the neck, tilts the head back,
and pours liquid down what is left of the

00:48:04.650 --> 00:48:06.320
throat of Felix Carter.

00:48:06.320 --> 00:48:09.520
The corpse reanimates into the living Dr.
Carter.

00:48:09.520 --> 00:48:13.869
Death has been removed from his body by liquid
from the Fountain of Youth that Calvin had

00:48:13.869 --> 00:48:17.470
acquired on a previous raid on a Foundation
site.

00:48:17.470 --> 00:48:22.550
Seeing that Dr. Carter is now alive, Calvin
takes out his pistol and shoots the doctor

00:48:22.550 --> 00:48:24.280
twice, killing him.

00:48:24.280 --> 00:48:28.310
Calvin picks up the body and throws it into
a bottomless pit at the base of the tower.

00:48:28.310 --> 00:48:31.480
Dr. Felix Carter’s body disappears from
sight.

00:48:31.480 --> 00:48:34.359
The Overseers’ deal with death is now broken.

00:48:34.359 --> 00:48:38.119
They are vulnerable and can be killed at last.

00:48:38.119 --> 00:48:43.840
Calvin smiles and begins to turn away from
the pit when he comes face to face with Death.

00:48:43.840 --> 00:48:46.790
She stands with her head cocked to the side
looking at Calvin.

00:48:46.790 --> 00:48:51.090
“So it is you who has broken the Overseers’
deal with me, Calvin Lucien.”

00:48:51.090 --> 00:48:52.170
Calvin takes a step back.

00:48:52.170 --> 00:48:54.960
Why didn’t she stop him from killing Felix
Carter?

00:48:54.960 --> 00:48:58.320
“Something festers at the heart of the council,”
Death says.

00:48:58.320 --> 00:48:59.890
“Something that will not die.

00:48:59.890 --> 00:49:04.810
I thought that, perhaps, if I had a seat at
their table, I could find it, make it die.

00:49:04.810 --> 00:49:05.840
But I couldn’t.

00:49:05.840 --> 00:49:10.280
There are things in this world beyond even
my reach, Calvin Lucien.”

00:49:10.280 --> 00:49:12.890
With that parting thought Death vanishes.

00:49:12.890 --> 00:49:17.540
The Killsquad contacts the Insurgency for
an evac and then makes their way to Japan

00:49:17.540 --> 00:49:21.670
where O5-12, also known as The Accountant,
has been working out of Tokyo.

00:49:21.670 --> 00:49:27.480
He is so proficient in mathematics and probability
that he can actually predict the future.

00:49:27.480 --> 00:49:30.670
Everything about the Accountant’s life,
down to the number of breaths and steps he

00:49:30.670 --> 00:49:35.680
takes each day, is predetermined based on
his own statistical models.

00:49:35.680 --> 00:49:38.230
This poses a problem for Calvin and his team.

00:49:38.230 --> 00:49:42.390
If The Accountant can see them coming, then
how can they possibly kill him?

00:49:42.390 --> 00:49:44.849
That night The Accountant steps out of his
car.

00:49:44.849 --> 00:49:46.380
He looks to the left and spots Adam.

00:49:46.380 --> 00:49:49.839
He has already predicted this man has hostile
intentions.

00:49:49.839 --> 00:49:54.230
The Accountant walks directly towards Adam,
and before he can react, throws the Killsquad

00:49:54.230 --> 00:49:55.230
member to the ground.

00:49:55.230 --> 00:49:59.330
Then he turns slightly and adjusts his watch
sending a glare directly into the window where

00:49:59.330 --> 00:50:02.800
Anthony has the Accountant in the sights of
his sniper rifle.

00:50:02.800 --> 00:50:06.630
Anthony fires, but misses, due to being blinded
by the glare.

00:50:06.630 --> 00:50:11.480
The Accountant is surprised that he just barely
had time to avoid being shot, normally he

00:50:11.480 --> 00:50:13.970
would be several steps ahead of anyone trying
to kill him.

00:50:13.970 --> 00:50:18.820
He turns his head and watches as Olivia helps
Adam up and they run down a nearby alley.

00:50:18.820 --> 00:50:22.270
The Accountant pursues them and corners the
Killsquad members in the alley.

00:50:22.270 --> 00:50:26.760
He pulls a gun to shoot Adam, but Olivia tackles
Adam behind a dumpster as the bullet hits

00:50:26.760 --> 00:50:29.780
the wall directly behind where Adam was standing.

00:50:29.780 --> 00:50:33.410
The Accountant can’t believe that he missed,
and that he was almost tricked into being

00:50:33.410 --> 00:50:35.710
captured by the Insurgency team.

00:50:35.710 --> 00:50:40.790
He senses uncertainty in his assailants actions
and runs away unable to predict exactly what

00:50:40.790 --> 00:50:42.350
they are planning to do.

00:50:42.350 --> 00:50:47.030
The Accountant climbs the stairs to a subway
station and boards the last car of the train.

00:50:47.030 --> 00:50:50.230
It is empty except for one man, Calvin Lucien.

00:50:50.230 --> 00:50:51.310
The Accountant is dumbfounded.

00:50:51.310 --> 00:50:53.220
“How are you here?” he screams.

00:50:53.220 --> 00:50:55.170
“I should have seen this coming!”

00:50:55.170 --> 00:50:56.170
Calvin stands up.

00:50:56.170 --> 00:50:59.050
He uses his thumb to flip a coin into the
air.

00:50:59.050 --> 00:51:03.210
On the way down he grabs it and smacks it
on the back of his opposing hand.

00:51:03.210 --> 00:51:04.330
Calvin smiles.

00:51:04.330 --> 00:51:09.220
The team has been making their decisions based
on the flip of a coin which introduced randomness

00:51:09.220 --> 00:51:14.130
into their actions that even this super advanced
mathematician could not account for.

00:51:14.130 --> 00:51:17.310
“Tell me where O5-11 is,” demands Calvin.

00:51:17.310 --> 00:51:19.970
The Accountant pauses, then shakes his head
no.

00:51:19.970 --> 00:51:24.589
If he’s going to die either way, then why
give any information to the Killsquad.

00:51:24.589 --> 00:51:28.130
Calvin flips the coin up in the air, catches
it, and looks at it.

00:51:28.130 --> 00:51:29.770
The coin is face up.

00:51:29.770 --> 00:51:32.940
Calvin lifts his pistol and shoots The Accountant
in the head.

00:51:32.940 --> 00:51:37.390
A few nights later Olivia stands on a balcony
outside of an art exhibit overlooking the

00:51:37.390 --> 00:51:38.670
city of Seattle.

00:51:38.670 --> 00:51:43.010
Anthony walks up behind her and tells her
that the Foundation is defeated but Olivia

00:51:43.010 --> 00:51:44.380
doesn’t understand how.

00:51:44.380 --> 00:51:47.820
“We broke the Overseers deal with death
and killed The Accountant, there is nothing

00:51:47.820 --> 00:51:48.820
more to do.

00:51:48.820 --> 00:51:51.620
We can go back to our normal lives” he tells
her.

00:51:51.620 --> 00:51:53.140
Olivia is skeptical though.

00:51:53.140 --> 00:51:54.570
What about the Eleventh Overseer?

00:51:54.570 --> 00:51:56.290
And his ability to…

00:51:56.290 --> 00:51:58.790
Olivia’s eyes suddenly open wide.

00:51:58.790 --> 00:52:01.339
She pulls out a knife and stabs it into Anthony’s
heart.

00:52:01.339 --> 00:52:03.770
The world around her begins to distort and
falls apart.

00:52:03.770 --> 00:52:09.550
It was a false reality created by O5-11, better
known as The Liar.

00:52:09.550 --> 00:52:12.050
Olivia wakes up next to Adam in a hotel room.

00:52:12.050 --> 00:52:13.990
She sits up in bed and rubs her eyes.

00:52:13.990 --> 00:52:16.030
What a weird dream, she thinks.

00:52:16.030 --> 00:52:18.630
Then she realizes it wasn’t a dream.

00:52:18.630 --> 00:52:19.950
She shakes Adam awake.

00:52:19.950 --> 00:52:24.359
Neither of them have any idea how they ended
up here, but they know it must be the doing

00:52:24.359 --> 00:52:29.220
of The Liar. they had planned for this though,
with Calvin having created a contingency plan.

00:52:29.220 --> 00:52:34.070
They pull out a laptop log in to view the
classified information Calvin left for them.

00:52:34.070 --> 00:52:38.670
Olivia begins to type but stops halfway through
her password and looks up from the screen.

00:52:38.670 --> 00:52:42.150
Olivia pulls out the gun that rests under
her pillow and shoots Adam.

00:52:42.150 --> 00:52:45.890
The false reality created by The Liar falls
apart around her.

00:52:45.890 --> 00:52:50.200
Olivia comes out of the previous lie and is
sitting across a table from Calvin.

00:52:50.200 --> 00:52:53.260
She immediately draws her pistol and points
it at Calvin's head.

00:52:53.260 --> 00:52:54.280
Is it really him?

00:52:54.280 --> 00:52:56.710
Or just another one of the Liar’s games?

00:52:56.710 --> 00:53:00.940
Calvin tries to talk Olivia down as she looks
around the room for inconsistencies that might

00:53:00.940 --> 00:53:04.420
tip her off that this is another lie, but
doesn’t find any.

00:53:04.420 --> 00:53:06.310
Olivia begins to relax.

00:53:06.310 --> 00:53:09.420
She tells Calvin that The Liar is trying to
get something from her.

00:53:09.420 --> 00:53:13.700
Maybe the Journal can tell them what he is
looking for, as long as she still has it.

00:53:13.700 --> 00:53:18.030
Olivia nods her head and holds out her wrist
where a subdermal chip with a copy of the

00:53:18.030 --> 00:53:19.810
Journal on it has been placed.

00:53:19.810 --> 00:53:24.280
Calvin looks at her wrist; the world around
them begins to dissipate as Calvin morphs

00:53:24.280 --> 00:53:25.470
into the Liar.

00:53:25.470 --> 00:53:29.050
Olivia wakes up in a hospital where she is
hooked up to an IV.

00:53:29.050 --> 00:53:33.010
Sitting across from her is a former Insurgency
agent named Sam Biel.

00:53:33.010 --> 00:53:35.450
He explains to her that he is The Liar.

00:53:35.450 --> 00:53:38.260
He was forced into becoming a monster by the
Foundation.

00:53:38.260 --> 00:53:43.000
They had manipulated him, but now he’s tired
of running and can’t do it anymore.

00:53:43.000 --> 00:53:44.660
She is free to go.

00:53:44.660 --> 00:53:47.470
Olivia hesitantly unhooks herself from the
IV.

00:53:47.470 --> 00:53:51.630
She walks out of the hospital room and proceeds
down a fluorescent lit hallway.

00:53:51.630 --> 00:53:55.099
As she walks away, she hears a gunshot from
the hospital room.

00:53:55.099 --> 00:53:58.990
As Olivia is in the hospital, Calvin and Adam
walk through a dense forest.

00:53:58.990 --> 00:54:01.349
They are searching for O5-10.

00:54:01.349 --> 00:54:05.600
The Journal indicates that the Tenth Overseer’s
identity within the Foundation is The Archivist.

00:54:05.600 --> 00:54:06.600
Calvin and Adam come upon a small clearing.

00:54:06.600 --> 00:54:10.290
In the middle of the clearing are two saplings
standing side by side.

00:54:10.290 --> 00:54:13.200
The void between the saplings shimmers.

00:54:13.200 --> 00:54:17.440
Calvin walks through the portal, and space
begins to warp and twist around him.

00:54:17.440 --> 00:54:23.580
His vision finally comes back into focus and
Calvin finds himself in another world.

00:54:23.580 --> 00:54:28.030
Adam enters the world behind Calvin, practically
knocking him over as he enters through the

00:54:28.030 --> 00:54:29.100
portal.

00:54:29.100 --> 00:54:30.480
This is the Wanderer’s Library.

00:54:30.480 --> 00:54:34.770
But it doesn’t look anything like they expected.

00:54:34.770 --> 00:54:39.750
Instead of rows of books, the Library is filled
with computer mainframes, humming with the

00:54:39.750 --> 00:54:44.470
collected knowledge of how to contain anomalies,
a critical backup.

00:54:44.470 --> 00:54:49.730
As the two look intently at the strange machines,
a figure in a silver robe suddenly steps out

00:54:49.730 --> 00:54:50.730
of the darkness.

00:54:50.730 --> 00:54:55.609
It’s tall and thin, and though it’s hood
is pulled down so that they can’t see its

00:54:55.609 --> 00:55:01.060
face, they can see that it’s hands are covered
in scales that have a slight, emerald tint.

00:55:01.060 --> 00:55:03.370
It is one of the Librarians.

00:55:03.370 --> 00:55:07.970
Calvin tells the Librarian that they are seeking
the Archivist, but the Librarian tells them

00:55:07.970 --> 00:55:10.870
that the Archivist is no longer in the library.

00:55:10.870 --> 00:55:16.500
She has broken her pact with the Serpent,
and eaten fruit from the forbidden trees.

00:55:16.500 --> 00:55:21.530
If they want to see her though, the Librarian
can take them to her.

00:55:21.530 --> 00:55:26.600
Calvin and Adam follow the Librarian down
a long staircase, passing by countless doors

00:55:26.600 --> 00:55:33.420
filled with books, scrolls, works of art,
an entire universe of knowledge.

00:55:33.420 --> 00:55:38.020
Eventually they reach the bottom of the stairs
where there stands a giant set of brass doors.

00:55:38.020 --> 00:55:43.880
Beyond the door, the librarian explains, is
the source of all knowledge.

00:55:43.880 --> 00:55:48.390
Before Calvin and Adam pass through the doors
though, Calvin turns to the Librarian.

00:55:48.390 --> 00:55:51.410
“Before we go in, I’d like to make a withdrawal”
he says.

00:55:51.410 --> 00:55:56.020
The librarian nods, and pulls a silver tube
out of its robe.

00:55:56.020 --> 00:55:59.600
It hands the tube to Adam and he looks it
over in his hands.

00:55:59.600 --> 00:56:03.980
He looks up to ask what this is, but the Librarian
has vanished.

00:56:03.980 --> 00:56:07.859
The doors then open and the two step through.

00:56:07.859 --> 00:56:11.740
Calvin and Adam feel as if they walk through
the same kind of portal that brought them

00:56:11.740 --> 00:56:17.800
to the library, and find that they have walked
into a lush green valley with two trees.

00:56:17.800 --> 00:56:21.230
Sitting underneath one of them is a woman
in a white dress.

00:56:21.230 --> 00:56:24.040
She is reading a book and eating a piece of
fruit.

00:56:24.040 --> 00:56:25.850
“Are you the Archivist?”

00:56:25.850 --> 00:56:26.869
Calvin asks.

00:56:26.869 --> 00:56:31.040
The woman nods yes and that’s all the confirmation
Calvin needs.

00:56:31.040 --> 00:56:36.150
He raises his pistol and fires,, but the bullet
passes right through The Archivist as if she

00:56:36.150 --> 00:56:37.190
wasn’t there.

00:56:37.190 --> 00:56:42.960
“Do you read?” the Archivist asks Calvin,
seemingly not phased by his attempts to shoot

00:56:42.960 --> 00:56:43.960
her.

00:56:43.960 --> 00:56:47.150
“I haven’t had much time recently” Calvin
replied.

00:56:47.150 --> 00:56:50.660
The Archivist explains that she’s read every
book in the library.

00:56:50.660 --> 00:56:55.420
The collected knowledge of the universe is
in the books, even one on how to allow bullets

00:56:55.420 --> 00:56:57.430
to pass through your body.

00:56:57.430 --> 00:57:00.130
She came here to find the secret to immortality.

00:57:00.130 --> 00:57:05.490
It’s her job to document everything that
happens in the world, and she can’t do that

00:57:05.490 --> 00:57:07.060
if she’s dead.

00:57:07.060 --> 00:57:11.210
She explains that she figured out that the
fruit that the Serpent forbade everyone to

00:57:11.210 --> 00:57:15.910
eat wasn’t actual fruit, but the knowledge
contained in the library.

00:57:15.910 --> 00:57:19.859
By having read every book, she had consumed
the fruit.

00:57:19.859 --> 00:57:24.890
She no longer needed the Serpent, because
she was the Serpent.

00:57:24.890 --> 00:57:29.240
The Archivist falls to the ground and begins
to writhe around, contorting her body as it

00:57:29.240 --> 00:57:30.730
starts to change.

00:57:30.730 --> 00:57:34.240
She begins to elongate as her limbs seemingly
disappear.

00:57:34.240 --> 00:57:39.579
The next thing Calvin and Adam know, they
are face to face with a giant snake.

00:57:39.579 --> 00:57:43.740
Calvin dodges as the serpent lunges at him
as Adam stands in the doorway firing at the

00:57:43.740 --> 00:57:48.260
snake with his pistol, but just like with
the Archivist’s human form, the bullets

00:57:48.260 --> 00:57:49.760
have no effect.

00:57:49.760 --> 00:57:53.510
The Serpent coils itself around Calvin and
begins to choke the life from him as Adam

00:57:53.510 --> 00:57:56.150
can only watch, helpless.

00:57:56.150 --> 00:57:59.470
Calvin cries out with his last breath “The
tube, Adam!

00:57:59.470 --> 00:58:01.140
Open the tube!”

00:58:01.140 --> 00:58:04.980
Adam takes the tube that was given to him
by the Librarian and opens the cap.

00:58:04.980 --> 00:58:10.640
A long, heavy spear slides out that looks
much too large to have ever fit inside.

00:58:10.640 --> 00:58:15.340
He drops the tube to the ground and watches
in amazement as it starts to transform, turning

00:58:15.340 --> 00:58:18.109
into what looks like a large harpoon gun.

00:58:18.109 --> 00:58:22.820
Adam knows what to do and places the giant
spear into the gun and points it at the Serpent.

00:58:22.820 --> 00:58:29.730
“You can’t kill me” the giant snake
says, “I’ve eaten from the tree of life!”

00:58:29.730 --> 00:58:34.280
Adam pulls the trigger and the huge spear
flies through the air, striking the serpent

00:58:34.280 --> 00:58:35.460
in the head.

00:58:35.460 --> 00:58:38.089
Adam runs to Calvin and helps him to his feet.

00:58:38.089 --> 00:58:42.990
They turn to look at the snake, but instead
of the menacing creature, it’s the Archivist

00:58:42.990 --> 00:58:49.750
once again, pinned against the tree she once
sat under, the spear sticking out of her skull.

00:58:49.750 --> 00:58:54.760
As the two stand, looking at the Archivist,
a tall, hooded, humanoid figure steps out

00:58:54.760 --> 00:58:56.420
from behind the tree.

00:58:56.420 --> 00:59:01.240
It looks similar to the Librarian except its
robe is a greenish color and it wears long

00:59:01.240 --> 00:59:02.570
black gloves.

00:59:02.570 --> 00:59:07.260
The creature pulls the spear out of the Archivist,
whose body slumps to the ground, and hands

00:59:07.260 --> 00:59:09.301
the spear to Calvin.

00:59:09.301 --> 00:59:10.301
“Who are you?”

00:59:10.301 --> 00:59:12.980
Calvin asks, but his question is ignored.

00:59:12.980 --> 00:59:15.589
After a moment, the figure finally speaks.

00:59:15.589 --> 00:59:21.470
“That spear you now hold is called the Spear
of the Non-Believer, it is an ancient weapon

00:59:21.470 --> 00:59:23.510
used to kill gods.

00:59:23.510 --> 00:59:27.560
It is odd that someone in this realm gave
you the spear.

00:59:27.560 --> 00:59:32.820
Even with it, I am not sure you will be able
to complete your quest Calvin Lucien, but

00:59:32.820 --> 00:59:34.740
we shall see.”

00:59:34.740 --> 00:59:39.290
There is a sudden flash of light and Calvin
and Adam find themselves transported back

00:59:39.290 --> 00:59:43.250
to the forest they had entered The Wanderer’s
Library from.

00:59:43.250 --> 00:59:48.520
A week later Calvin and Anthony track down
O5-9, who in the council, is known as The

00:59:48.520 --> 00:59:49.520
Outsider.

00:59:49.520 --> 00:59:53.460
She isn’t hard to find and it seems as if
she actually wanted to be found.

00:59:53.460 --> 00:59:56.750
They find her sitting outside of her burnt
down family home.

00:59:56.750 --> 01:00:01.070
The journal had listed this as her address,
but Calvin doubted that she would be here.

01:00:01.070 --> 01:00:06.520
At most he hoped to find a clue to her whereabouts,
but here she was, sitting in the ashes of

01:00:06.520 --> 01:00:07.570
her home.

01:00:07.570 --> 01:00:09.890
Without turning around The Outsider began
speaking.

01:00:09.890 --> 01:00:12.380
“The council just used me you know,” she
says.

01:00:12.380 --> 01:00:16.010
“They took away my academic career, my friends,
and my life.

01:00:16.010 --> 01:00:20.040
They made me conduct research for them that
compromised everything I stood for, and now

01:00:20.040 --> 01:00:21.640
here I am, with nothing.”

01:00:21.640 --> 01:00:23.599
The Outsider lets out a sigh.

01:00:23.599 --> 01:00:25.720
She asks Calvin if he’s afraid of death.

01:00:25.720 --> 01:00:28.250
Calvin shakes his head and responds, “no.”

01:00:28.250 --> 01:00:31.460
The Outsider slumps forward and Calvin walks
around to face her.

01:00:31.460 --> 01:00:32.920
She is covered in blood.

01:00:32.920 --> 01:00:35.000
Her eyes move to look up at Calvin.

01:00:35.000 --> 01:00:39.630
“You’re lying,” she says as she dies
from self inflicted wounds.

01:00:39.630 --> 01:00:43.890
Calvin and Anthony cross O5-9 off of the list
and head back to the car.

01:00:43.890 --> 01:00:48.119
As they walk, Anthony says what’s been on
everyones’ mind the last few days.

01:00:48.119 --> 01:00:49.470
“The easy part is done.

01:00:49.470 --> 01:00:51.410
It will only get harder from here.

01:00:51.410 --> 01:00:55.570
We know O5-8 is in his castle, and I’m sure
we can get in, but I’m not sure we’ll

01:00:55.570 --> 01:00:56.570
make it out alive.”

01:00:56.570 --> 01:00:58.130
“I know,” replies Calvin.

01:00:58.130 --> 01:01:02.400
“But if we are going to save the world,
we must eliminate the rest of the Overseers,

01:01:02.400 --> 01:01:04.430
even if it means sacrificing our own lives.”

01:01:04.430 --> 01:01:09.339
They get in the car and drive off into the
blood red sunset to pick up the rest of the

01:01:09.339 --> 01:01:12.480
Killsquad team before their next mission.

01:01:12.480 --> 01:01:16.579
Calvin Lucien leads the Killsquad team through
mud and freezing rain.

01:01:16.579 --> 01:01:21.750
In front of them looms the fortress of Baron
Leeman Hoadley, the Eighth Overseer.

01:01:21.750 --> 01:01:26.050
The team has already been through a lot: from
breaking the Overseer Council’s deal with

01:01:26.050 --> 01:01:32.790
death by eliminating O5-13, to using the Spear
of the Non-Believer to kill the god like Archivist,

01:01:32.790 --> 01:01:34.030
O5-10.

01:01:34.030 --> 01:01:37.850
The hunting of Overseers has taken a toll
on the Killsquad.

01:01:37.850 --> 01:01:43.000
O5-12 almost killed Adam, and Olivia was stuck
in what seemed like an endless mind game with

01:01:43.000 --> 01:01:44.420
O5-11.

01:01:44.420 --> 01:01:49.520
The first five Overseers were eliminated,
but the words that the Ninth Overseer spoke

01:01:49.520 --> 01:01:56.170
to Calvin Lucien before she died still run
through his mind: are you afraid of death?

01:01:56.170 --> 01:02:00.190
Now the Killsquad is about to infiltrate one
of the most heavily guarded facilities in

01:02:00.190 --> 01:02:03.450
the world to eliminate the Eighth Overseer.

01:02:03.450 --> 01:02:07.800
Upon reaching the castle the team is surprised
to find the structure in ruin.

01:02:07.800 --> 01:02:11.250
No one is supposed to know the location of
O5-8 though.

01:02:11.250 --> 01:02:14.770
The fortress was supposed to be practically
impregnable.

01:02:14.770 --> 01:02:17.670
They storm the castle of O5-8 all the same.

01:02:17.670 --> 01:02:23.220
The journal Calvin possesses that contains
information about the members of the SCP Foundation’s

01:02:23.220 --> 01:02:29.470
powerful O5 Council identifies him as a former
industrialist named Baron Leeman Hoadley.

01:02:29.470 --> 01:02:34.730
With his vast wealth, Hoadley funded the Foundation
at the start and was considered the unofficial

01:02:34.730 --> 01:02:40.710
leader of the council in its early days with
immense control over the actions of the organization.

01:02:40.710 --> 01:02:44.500
The Killsquad makes their way through the
dimly lit hallways of the castle.

01:02:44.500 --> 01:02:48.320
As they turn the corner they are surprised
to find the charred remains of Baron Leeman

01:02:48.320 --> 01:02:50.180
Hoadley’s bodyguards.

01:02:50.180 --> 01:02:55.160
It seems that someone or something has gotten
to Hoadley before they could.

01:02:55.160 --> 01:02:58.760
The team makes their way to the main chamber
and breaches the door.

01:02:58.760 --> 01:03:02.280
Laying by a still lit fireplace is O5-8.

01:03:02.280 --> 01:03:06.420
The Killsquad scan the room to make sure the
killer isn’t still in there with them.

01:03:06.420 --> 01:03:08.870
Adam walks over to the body and examines it.

01:03:08.870 --> 01:03:12.359
He quickly realizes that Hoadley hasn’t
been murdered at all.

01:03:12.359 --> 01:03:17.500
He sees that Barron Hoadley’s body has been
drastically modified using anomalous technology.

01:03:17.500 --> 01:03:22.630
The Overseer used his immortality to modify
almost every part of his body to make himself

01:03:22.630 --> 01:03:24.170
stronger.

01:03:24.170 --> 01:03:28.070
Unfortunately for Baron Hoadley, when the
Overseers’ deal with death was broken by

01:03:28.070 --> 01:03:32.390
Calvin, the modifications to his body slowly
tore him apart.

01:03:32.390 --> 01:03:36.920
His regular body could no longer support all
of the modifications, and what once made him

01:03:36.920 --> 01:03:41.440
practically invincible became the very thing
that destroyed him.

01:03:41.440 --> 01:03:45.810
The team leaves the castle and crosses O5-8
off of their list.

01:03:45.810 --> 01:03:48.260
On their way out Adam pulls Calvin aside.

01:03:48.260 --> 01:03:52.230
He has the feeling that Anthony hasn’t been
completely honest with the rest of the team.

01:03:52.230 --> 01:03:55.750
He had the feeling that Antony was hiding
something from them.

01:03:55.750 --> 01:03:57.869
Calvin had had similar thoughts recently.

01:03:57.869 --> 01:04:02.151
He pushes Anthony for more information about
his past and Anthony reveals that he’s over

01:04:02.151 --> 01:04:04.230
one hundred years old.

01:04:04.230 --> 01:04:08.920
The vial of water from the Fountain of Youth
that Calvin has was not the only one.

01:04:08.920 --> 01:04:14.070
Early in his career with the Insurgency he
had confiscated other vials from a Foundation

01:04:14.070 --> 01:04:15.119
site.

01:04:15.119 --> 01:04:18.550
His squad drank the water and it extended
their lives.

01:04:18.550 --> 01:04:22.380
He asks Calvin what he plans on doing with
his water from the fountain.

01:04:22.380 --> 01:04:25.140
“I’m going to destroy it,” Calvin tells
him.

01:04:25.140 --> 01:04:27.270
Anthony agrees with this plan.

01:04:27.270 --> 01:04:31.510
Once you drink from the fountain of youth
you may extend your life, but a part of you

01:04:31.510 --> 01:04:33.280
dies at the same time.

01:04:33.280 --> 01:04:38.579
“Vibrancy of the senses disappears, leading
to a seemingly shallow life.”

01:04:38.579 --> 01:04:42.870
If Anthony could go back and do it again,
he never would have drank the water.

01:04:42.870 --> 01:04:47.359
Calvin receives intel from the Insurgency
that the Seventh Overseer is in a small town

01:04:47.359 --> 01:04:48.660
in Cambodia.

01:04:48.660 --> 01:04:53.310
The Killsquad makes their way to the village
and surveys the area, hoping to get a glimpse

01:04:53.310 --> 01:04:56.320
at the Overseer who is code named Green.

01:04:56.320 --> 01:05:01.310
As the team conducts reconsiance, Anthony
tells them he thinks this mission is a setup.

01:05:01.310 --> 01:05:04.569
It is too remote, and there are so many unknown
variables.

01:05:04.569 --> 01:05:09.530
But, Calvin is convinced that this might be
their only chance to kill Green.

01:05:09.530 --> 01:05:13.240
Since Green arrived in the area there has
been nonstop chaos.

01:05:13.240 --> 01:05:18.180
She has destabilized the local governments
and now the area is in all out war.

01:05:18.180 --> 01:05:23.010
The team weaves through narrow passageways
between houses and buildings, trying to make

01:05:23.010 --> 01:05:26.780
their way to the central compound where Green
is located.

01:05:26.780 --> 01:05:28.690
Suddenly a mob starts to form.

01:05:28.690 --> 01:05:31.410
They are getting closer and closer to the
team.

01:05:31.410 --> 01:05:36.730
In a quick decision to avoid being seen, Calvin
orders everyone into a nearby building.

01:05:36.730 --> 01:05:39.510
Before Anthony can follow, the mob rounds
the corner.

01:05:39.510 --> 01:05:42.400
They spot Anthony and he’s forced to flee.

01:05:42.400 --> 01:05:47.020
Calvin, Olivia, and Adam watch as the mob
chases after Anthony, but they have to keep

01:05:47.020 --> 01:05:48.020
moving.

01:05:48.020 --> 01:05:52.040
Calvin knows that Anthony can take care of
himself, and they are too close to their goal

01:05:52.040 --> 01:05:53.400
to stop now.

01:05:53.400 --> 01:05:57.609
Calvin slowly opens the front door of the
house they are hiding in and peers out.

01:05:57.609 --> 01:06:01.890
The coast looks clear, so he signals Olivia
and Adam to follow him.

01:06:01.890 --> 01:06:05.910
Before they can step out into the street,
a gas canister enters through the cracked

01:06:05.910 --> 01:06:06.910
doorway.

01:06:06.910 --> 01:06:09.960
The room fills with sleeping gas and the team
passes out.

01:06:09.960 --> 01:06:15.130
When they awake, they are tied up in a large
room with marble vaulted ceilings.

01:06:15.130 --> 01:06:17.900
O5-7 is standing in front of Calvin.

01:06:17.900 --> 01:06:20.470
She smiles wickedly while holding a knife.

01:06:20.470 --> 01:06:24.990
She compliments Calvin on what he and his
team have been able to do so far.

01:06:24.990 --> 01:06:28.680
No one believed they could pull off even a
fraction of what they have.

01:06:28.680 --> 01:06:30.930
But now she has an offer for Calvin.

01:06:30.930 --> 01:06:35.860
She points towards Adam and Olivia and tells
Calvin he must choose one of them to die.

01:06:35.860 --> 01:06:40.220
If he doesn’t, she’ll kill the leader
of the rioters and plunge another part of

01:06:40.220 --> 01:06:42.030
the country into chaos.

01:06:42.030 --> 01:06:44.569
“Screw you” is Calvin’s response.

01:06:44.569 --> 01:06:46.490
“Very well,” utters Green.

01:06:46.490 --> 01:06:48.290
“Have it your way.”

01:06:48.290 --> 01:06:53.020
She assassinates the leader being held in
her compound, then turns back to Calvin.

01:06:53.020 --> 01:06:57.510
She now threatens to torture his team until
Calvin makes a choice of who to kill.

01:06:57.510 --> 01:07:01.280
Green slashes Adam’s cheek with her knife
as Calvin screams for Green to leave his team

01:07:01.280 --> 01:07:03.020
alone and torture him instead.

01:07:03.020 --> 01:07:04.660
Green just smiles.

01:07:04.660 --> 01:07:10.320
“I am going to enjoy killing your friends
while you watch, as you have killed so many

01:07:10.320 --> 01:07:12.730
of my Overseers on the council.”

01:07:12.730 --> 01:07:16.130
She reaches up in the air with the knife above
Adam’s head.

01:07:16.130 --> 01:07:20.860
Before she can plunge the knife through his
skull a bullet passes through her hand, causing

01:07:20.860 --> 01:07:22.339
her to drop the knife.

01:07:22.339 --> 01:07:27.520
Anthony kneels on a rooftop across the courtyard,
smoking sniper rifle still pointed at Green

01:07:27.520 --> 01:07:28.800
who runs.

01:07:28.800 --> 01:07:32.490
Calvin uses the dropped knife to cut his ropes
and chases after Green.

01:07:32.490 --> 01:07:36.099
He follows her to the roof where he watches
as she boards a helicopter.

01:07:36.099 --> 01:07:40.430
The aircraft lifts off as Anthony fires at
it from his original position, but does no

01:07:40.430 --> 01:07:42.060
serious damage.

01:07:42.060 --> 01:07:46.920
In the plaza below the mob that had separated
the team earlier becomes restless.

01:07:46.920 --> 01:07:51.020
There is complete chaos and someone fires
a rocket at the fleeing helicopter.

01:07:51.020 --> 01:07:55.230
The rocket hits the tail of the aircraft,
sending it crashing into the plaza full of

01:07:55.230 --> 01:07:58.610
rioters below as the crowd flees from the
scene.

01:07:58.610 --> 01:08:01.869
Calvin makes his way towards the wreckage
and reaches the wreckage at the same time

01:08:01.869 --> 01:08:03.000
Anthony does.

01:08:03.000 --> 01:08:07.440
Calvin looks at him, smiles, and thanks him
for saving his life.

01:08:07.440 --> 01:08:12.210
Anthony smiles back but before he can say
anything, a gunshot rings out and a bullet

01:08:12.210 --> 01:08:13.840
rips through his neck.

01:08:13.840 --> 01:08:19.189
Calvin turns to see where it came from and
is horrified to see the burning body of O5-8.

01:08:19.189 --> 01:08:25.319
Her skin has been charred black, but in her
burnt hand she holds a gun.

01:08:25.319 --> 01:08:30.559
What’s left of her lips curl back in a sinister
grin as she fires again and hits Anthony in

01:08:30.559 --> 01:08:31.600
the chest.

01:08:31.600 --> 01:08:33.400
He falls to the ground.

01:08:33.400 --> 01:08:39.069
Calvin runs to him and pulls his gun out to
shoot O5-8, but she is already dead.

01:08:39.069 --> 01:08:43.089
Calvin holds his dying teammate as blood pours
out of his neck and chest.

01:08:43.089 --> 01:08:44.719
But Calvin can stop this.

01:08:44.719 --> 01:08:47.190
He pulls out the vial of water from the Fountain
of Youth.

01:08:47.190 --> 01:08:48.560
“No,” winces Anthony.

01:08:48.560 --> 01:08:50.210
“I have lived long enough.

01:08:50.210 --> 01:08:55.089
Thank you my friend, I will see you in whatever
lies beyond this life.”

01:08:55.089 --> 01:08:59.509
Anthony’s chest rises then falls, it does
not rise again.

01:08:59.509 --> 01:09:04.400
Olivia and Adam round the corner to see Calvin
holding the lifeless body of their teammate,

01:09:04.400 --> 01:09:06.289
tears flowing from his eyes.

01:09:06.289 --> 01:09:10.759
The team holds a small ceremony and burial
for Anthony, but they are only halfway through

01:09:10.759 --> 01:09:13.409
their mission, and can’t stop now.

01:09:13.409 --> 01:09:17.799
They fly back to the United States where an
undercover Insurgency agent named Kowalski

01:09:17.799 --> 01:09:22.420
informs them that O5-6 is already aware they
are after him.

01:09:22.420 --> 01:09:28.040
This Overseer is code named The American because
he has the power of the entire U.S. Military

01:09:28.040 --> 01:09:29.409
at his fingertips.

01:09:29.409 --> 01:09:32.529
The Killsquad scouts the base where The American
is located.

01:09:32.529 --> 01:09:37.229
Kowalski warns them of a crate that was recently
brought to the base from Site-19.

01:09:37.229 --> 01:09:40.779
The American showed great interest in whatever
was in the container.

01:09:40.779 --> 01:09:44.219
The group sets up a camp on a hill overlooking
the base.

01:09:44.219 --> 01:09:49.049
As the sun slowly rises the next day, the
Killsquad is spotted by a drone and forced

01:09:49.049 --> 01:09:51.339
to hop in their Jeep and try to run.

01:09:51.339 --> 01:09:55.830
They make their way down the hill, finding
themselves in the valley below with no clear

01:09:55.830 --> 01:09:56.830
exit.

01:09:56.830 --> 01:10:00.679
In front of them lands a helicopter as humvees
roar into the canyon behind them.

01:10:00.679 --> 01:10:02.239
The team is surrounded.

01:10:02.239 --> 01:10:05.999
A Jeep pulls up and O5-6 steps out.

01:10:05.999 --> 01:10:11.670
He introduces himself as Rufus King, member
of the Overseer Council, but an American citizen

01:10:11.670 --> 01:10:13.400
first and foremost.

01:10:13.400 --> 01:10:16.520
All he really wants is to protect the country
he loves.

01:10:16.520 --> 01:10:21.019
“Thanks to you, I have lost my immortality
and can no longer effectively protect the

01:10:21.019 --> 01:10:24.360
United States anymore,” the American says
to Calvin.

01:10:24.360 --> 01:10:30.360
“But I am willing to make a deal… your
freedom for the Spear of the Non-Believer.

01:10:30.360 --> 01:10:34.570
Rumor has it that you have the spear in your
possession, and you used it to kill the Archivist.

01:10:34.570 --> 01:10:38.300
If you give me the spear I will let you go.”

01:10:38.300 --> 01:10:39.699
“No,” replies Calvin.

01:10:39.699 --> 01:10:43.079
“I will never give an Overseer the means
to cause more destruction.

01:10:43.079 --> 01:10:44.900
The spear stays with us.”

01:10:44.900 --> 01:10:48.210
“Very well,” the American says with a
frown.

01:10:48.210 --> 01:10:53.260
“Then I suppose my only other option is
to take it from you, but not without giving

01:10:53.260 --> 01:10:54.939
you a fair chance.

01:10:54.939 --> 01:10:57.499
Run Calvin Lucien.

01:10:57.499 --> 01:11:05.429
Run as fast as you can, I will be coming for
you.”

01:11:05.429 --> 01:11:10.739
The American turns and walks towards the container
from Site-19, which is being lowered from

01:11:10.739 --> 01:11:13.150
a helicopter hovering above them.

01:11:13.150 --> 01:11:16.380
Calvin sprints back to the Jeep with the other
members of his team.

01:11:16.380 --> 01:11:23.030
As they drive away they hear a horrible, guttural,
screech from whatever was inside the container.

01:11:23.030 --> 01:11:27.969
After a few moments the army begins to pursue
them, out in front of the military force is

01:11:27.969 --> 01:11:30.949
O5-6 riding SCP-682.

01:11:30.949 --> 01:11:38.030
He is using a black whip to urge the creature
forward, and they’re gaining on the Killsquad…

01:11:38.030 --> 01:11:39.289
fast.

01:11:39.289 --> 01:11:45.610
A row of vehicles pulls up beside The American
and SCP-682, then something strange happens.

01:11:45.610 --> 01:11:49.460
A man appears in front of the oncoming forces
led by the American.

01:11:49.460 --> 01:11:53.179
The man’s skin bulges and seems to be moving
from within.

01:11:53.179 --> 01:11:56.019
The skin of the man sloughs from his body.

01:11:56.019 --> 01:12:02.610
The infection that is SCP-610 erupts out of
him and onto the soldiers in a nearby Jeep.

01:12:02.610 --> 01:12:06.559
SCP-610 begins to infect and consume everyone
around it.

01:12:06.559 --> 01:12:12.320
Suddenly, there are thousands of instances
of SCP-610 coming from the mountain side,

01:12:12.320 --> 01:12:13.699
flooding into the valley.

01:12:13.699 --> 01:12:17.570
They close in around the army and O5-6.

01:12:17.570 --> 01:12:21.469
The American begins fighting off the flesh
eating creatures from the back of SCP-682,

01:12:21.469 --> 01:12:24.699
but he becomes overwhelmed.

01:12:24.699 --> 01:12:28.289
He can no longer focus on pursuing Calvin
and his team.

01:12:28.289 --> 01:12:31.019
From the back of the Jeep Olivia pulls out
her rifle.

01:12:31.019 --> 01:12:33.030
She aims and fires.

01:12:33.030 --> 01:12:35.150
The bullet hits The American in the chest.

01:12:35.150 --> 01:12:42.250
He is flung off the back of SCP-682 and engulfed
in a sea of SCP-610 creatures.

01:12:42.250 --> 01:12:47.030
The Killsquad continues to drive, trying to
put as much distance between themselves and

01:12:47.030 --> 01:12:50.189
the SCP-610 infestation as possible.

01:12:50.189 --> 01:12:53.170
But then Calvin suddenly slams on the breaks.

01:12:53.170 --> 01:12:57.199
Standing in front of them is a man in a black
suit and bow tie.

01:12:57.199 --> 01:13:01.449
He introduces himself as Blackbird, the Fifth
Overseer.

01:13:01.449 --> 01:13:06.280
According to the journal his actual name is
Mortimer J. Denning Von Kronecker.

01:13:06.280 --> 01:13:09.170
He stands in front of the Jeep with a menacing
grin.

01:13:09.170 --> 01:13:13.449
“You have been causing a lot of trouble,”
he says looking at Calvin.

01:13:13.449 --> 01:13:15.040
Olivia swings her gun around.

01:13:15.040 --> 01:13:19.989
“Please my dear, that won’t help you,”
Von Kronecker says.

01:13:19.989 --> 01:13:22.750
He pulls out a knife and stabs himself through
the neck.

01:13:22.750 --> 01:13:25.570
He falls to the ground apparently dead.

01:13:25.570 --> 01:13:31.329
There is a gust of wind, a whiff of ozone,
and an identical copy, and still very much

01:13:31.329 --> 01:13:34.510
alive, Von Kronecker lands next to his own
dead body.

01:13:34.510 --> 01:13:37.280
“See what I mean,” he says.

01:13:37.280 --> 01:13:38.820
Olivia lowers her rifle.

01:13:38.820 --> 01:13:43.289
“Come with me; I have something to show
you,” the Blackbird beccons.

01:13:43.289 --> 01:13:48.570
Seeing no other option Calvin, Olivia, and
Adam exit the Jeep and follow the Blackbird.

01:13:48.570 --> 01:13:51.139
As they walk, the world changes around them.

01:13:51.139 --> 01:13:56.229
The desert mountains fade away into blackness
and they find themselves in a near-apocalyptic

01:13:56.229 --> 01:13:57.229
London.

01:13:57.229 --> 01:14:03.059
“Ah, it’s good to be home,” the Blackbird
says as they emerge onto a cobblestone street.

01:14:03.059 --> 01:14:08.189
“You cannot stop the Overseers plans, however,
I can give you an alternative.

01:14:08.189 --> 01:14:10.699
Let’s see if any of you will take it.”

01:14:10.699 --> 01:14:13.780
In front of each Killsquad member appears
a door.

01:14:13.780 --> 01:14:18.449
They have an uncontrollable urge to open their
respective door and walk through.

01:14:18.449 --> 01:14:23.650
The Blackbird stands smiling as he watches
Calvin, Olivia, and Adam enter each of their

01:14:23.650 --> 01:14:24.780
portals.

01:14:24.780 --> 01:14:26.679
Adam enters his door and looks around.

01:14:26.679 --> 01:14:28.340
He is in Portland.

01:14:28.340 --> 01:14:30.119
His parents walk into the room.

01:14:30.119 --> 01:14:33.840
In this universe his family has been granted
asylum.

01:14:33.840 --> 01:14:37.699
Adam never has to interact with any SCPs or
the Foundation.

01:14:37.699 --> 01:14:39.880
He is free to live a normal life.

01:14:39.880 --> 01:14:42.190
From the kitchen comes Calvin wearing an apron.

01:14:42.190 --> 01:14:44.360
He is holding a steaming pot.

01:14:44.360 --> 01:14:46.999
Adam locks eyes with Calvin who smiles at
him.

01:14:46.999 --> 01:14:51.489
The Blackbird whispers into Adam’s ear,
“in this reality both of your parents and

01:14:51.489 --> 01:14:53.519
siblings are still alive.

01:14:53.519 --> 01:14:59.199
Also, the man you love loves you back, you
and Calvin could be married if you stayed

01:14:59.199 --> 01:15:01.389
here, wouldn’t that be nice?”

01:15:01.389 --> 01:15:03.110
Olivia enters her door.

01:15:03.110 --> 01:15:04.610
She is on the deck of a yacht.

01:15:04.610 --> 01:15:07.469
At the bow sits an easel with art supplies.

01:15:07.469 --> 01:15:11.199
The man that Olivia once loved walks across
the deck towards her.

01:15:11.199 --> 01:15:16.749
The Blackbird looms over her, “in this reality
you didn’t accidentally kill him.

01:15:16.749 --> 01:15:19.400
This could be your happily ever after.

01:15:19.400 --> 01:15:20.820
Wouldn’t that be nice?”

01:15:20.820 --> 01:15:22.590
Calvin steps through his door.

01:15:22.590 --> 01:15:25.119
He is in a grassy clearing near a lake.

01:15:25.119 --> 01:15:30.380
The Blackbird hisses in Calvin’s ear, “I’m
giving you the opportunity to save your mother

01:15:30.380 --> 01:15:32.360
this time Calvin.

01:15:32.360 --> 01:15:38.030
You were just a scared little boy, but in
this reality you can be brave.

01:15:38.030 --> 01:15:41.460
You can actually save your mother from her
fate.”

01:15:41.460 --> 01:15:42.460
“No!”

01:15:42.460 --> 01:15:43.460
Calvin screams.

01:15:43.460 --> 01:15:44.479
“This isn’t real!”

01:15:44.479 --> 01:15:46.119
The Blackbird cackles.

01:15:46.119 --> 01:15:48.709
Calvin looks away from the lake and towards
the treeline.

01:15:48.709 --> 01:15:52.840
Hidden in the shadows he can just barely make
out a hooded figure.

01:15:52.840 --> 01:15:54.119
Calvin walks towards it.

01:15:54.119 --> 01:15:57.499
The Blackbird follows, he is screaming at
the person in the treeline.

01:15:57.499 --> 01:15:59.639
“I was only trying to help!”

01:15:59.639 --> 01:16:03.269
The hooded figure reaches out and hands Calvin
a metal tube.

01:16:03.269 --> 01:16:06.429
He opens it to find a set of eyeglasses inside.

01:16:06.429 --> 01:16:09.010
Calvin puts them on and turns to look at the
Blackbird.

01:16:09.010 --> 01:16:10.939
He steps back in horror.

01:16:10.939 --> 01:16:14.300
The glasses have revealed the true form of
the Blackbird.

01:16:14.300 --> 01:16:19.530
He is a winged, pseudo-avian, monstrosity
full of rage.

01:16:19.530 --> 01:16:23.630
The mysterious hooded figure directs Calvin
to open the tube again.

01:16:23.630 --> 01:16:28.479
Inside is an interdimensional fishing line
made by Dr. Wondertainment, and white wiffle

01:16:28.479 --> 01:16:29.650
ball bat.

01:16:29.650 --> 01:16:34.059
Calvin grabs the fishing line and wraps it
around O5-5’s leg.

01:16:34.059 --> 01:16:38.059
The Blackbird flies into the air trying to
get away from Calvin, but Calvin wraps the

01:16:38.059 --> 01:16:40.570
other end of the fishing line around his arm.

01:16:40.570 --> 01:16:45.380
The Blackbird begins to jump from dimension
to dimension trying to get rid of Calvin.

01:16:45.380 --> 01:16:52.499
They appear on the deck of SCP-455, in Site-19
where SCP-682 walks freely, in the dead world

01:16:52.499 --> 01:16:55.020
of SCP-2935.

01:16:55.020 --> 01:17:00.099
Every time they stop in a new dimension, Calvin
takes the opportunity to attack the Blackbird

01:17:00.099 --> 01:17:01.199
with the bat.

01:17:01.199 --> 01:17:04.459
And it seems that he is slowly weakening the
monster.

01:17:04.459 --> 01:17:09.489
They finally land at the bottom of a Deepwell
Foundation containment site, where the Darkbody

01:17:09.489 --> 01:17:13.400
that is SCP-001 is contained.

01:17:13.400 --> 01:17:17.829
Standing in front of the containment field
is Alison Chao, The Black Queen, whose sole

01:17:17.829 --> 01:17:20.479
mission is to destroy the Foundation.

01:17:20.479 --> 01:17:22.139
“You!” cries the Blackbird.

01:17:22.139 --> 01:17:25.550
“You are the one who has been helping Lucien!”

01:17:25.550 --> 01:17:27.280
The Black Queen nods her head.

01:17:27.280 --> 01:17:32.999
“Yes, I have been helping Calvin Lucien
to eliminate you and the other Overseers.

01:17:32.999 --> 01:17:34.659
The Foundation must fall.”

01:17:34.659 --> 01:17:36.189
“You are nothing!

01:17:36.189 --> 01:17:37.869
You cannot stop me!

01:17:37.869 --> 01:17:41.639
I am The Black King!” screams O5-5.

01:17:41.639 --> 01:17:44.229
Alison Chao sighs.

01:17:44.229 --> 01:17:49.429
She pushes a button on the panel next to her,
shutting down the array containing the Darkbody.

01:17:49.429 --> 01:17:56.120
Out of the cloud of dust appears SCP-001,
a massive black creature who seemed to absorb

01:17:56.120 --> 01:17:57.210
all light.

01:17:57.210 --> 01:17:58.210
“No!

01:17:58.210 --> 01:18:00.380
Stop!” shrieks the Blackbird.

01:18:00.380 --> 01:18:05.040
SCP-001 does not move, but the room begins
to shake.

01:18:05.040 --> 01:18:10.500
The Blackbird continues to scream as his body
folds in on itself until he is reduced to

01:18:10.500 --> 01:18:14.880
a single superheated point, and then blinks
out of existence.

01:18:14.880 --> 01:18:20.730
Alison Chao then reactivates the containment
array, sealing 001 away once again.

01:18:20.730 --> 01:18:25.550
“I will return you to your reality along
with your friends,” says the Black Queen.

01:18:25.550 --> 01:18:29.130
“But perhaps our paths shall cross again
Calvin Lucien.”

01:18:29.130 --> 01:18:33.349
There is a bright flash of light and Calvin
finds himself on a private jet sitting next

01:18:33.349 --> 01:18:35.179
to Olivia and Adam.

01:18:35.179 --> 01:18:38.900
They are all shaken, but the Blackbird is
dead.

01:18:38.900 --> 01:18:41.019
O5-5 has been eliminated.

01:18:41.019 --> 01:18:45.630
The three members of the team sit silently,
still pondering what might have been if they

01:18:45.630 --> 01:18:47.860
stayed in the alternate realities.

01:18:47.860 --> 01:18:52.219
Suddenly, the phone on the plane begins to
ring, breaking the silence.

01:18:52.219 --> 01:18:53.369
Calvin picks it up.

01:18:53.369 --> 01:18:55.389
On the other line is the Fourth Overseer.

01:18:55.389 --> 01:19:00.219
He has contacted Calvin to discuss surrendering
to the Insurgency.

01:19:00.219 --> 01:19:04.189
Unfortunately, things do not always go as
planned.

01:19:04.189 --> 01:19:11.449
Calvin Lucien is about to make the most difficult
and dangerous decision of his life.

01:19:11.449 --> 01:19:18.570
Aaron Siegel, better known to Foundation members
as O5-1, descends into the abyss of a Deepwell

01:19:18.570 --> 01:19:19.570
site.

01:19:19.570 --> 01:19:24.780
He exits the elevator and peers into the optical
scanner to unlock the reinforced door.

01:19:24.780 --> 01:19:26.590
Inside the room is Mobile Task Force Tau-5…

01:19:26.590 --> 01:19:29.170
Samsara.

01:19:29.170 --> 01:19:35.369
Aaron Siegel refers to these immortal cyborg
clones, created from the flesh of a dead god,

01:19:35.369 --> 01:19:37.280
as his Red Right Hand.

01:19:37.280 --> 01:19:42.171
“Your mission is to eliminate the traitor
O5-4, and to find the insurgents who have

01:19:42.171 --> 01:19:44.739
been killing the members of the Overseer Council.”

01:19:44.739 --> 01:19:47.309
The cyborgs stand at attention.

01:19:47.309 --> 01:19:48.309
“Now!”

01:19:48.309 --> 01:19:49.440
Aaron Siegel screams.

01:19:49.440 --> 01:19:54.320
The soldiers of the Red Right Hand march out
the door to start their mission.

01:19:54.320 --> 01:19:59.300
Aaron Siegel pauses for a moment and then
slams his fist against the wall in frustration.

01:19:59.300 --> 01:20:03.630
He has lost nine Overseers to Calvin Lucien
and his Kill Squad team.

01:20:03.630 --> 01:20:09.099
They have been somehow overcoming the odds
each time, and eliminating each Overseer they

01:20:09.099 --> 01:20:10.099
track down.

01:20:10.099 --> 01:20:12.630
It wasn’t supposed to end this way.

01:20:12.630 --> 01:20:15.690
Aaron Siegel vows to kill them all.

01:20:15.690 --> 01:20:18.989
Calvin Lucien, meanwhile, sits on a private
jet with Adam and Olivia.

01:20:18.989 --> 01:20:23.489
He had just hung up the phone after a conversation
with O5-4.

01:20:23.489 --> 01:20:27.679
The Overseer known as the Ambassador wants
to surrender to the Insurgency.

01:20:27.679 --> 01:20:32.130
There’s a good chance this is a trap, but
Calvin has decided to meet with the Ambassador

01:20:32.130 --> 01:20:33.769
all the same.

01:20:33.769 --> 01:20:36.820
Calvin drops off Adam and Olivia at an Insurgency
base.

01:20:36.820 --> 01:20:42.090
They still haven’t fully recovered from
the previous mission with O5-5, known as the

01:20:42.090 --> 01:20:43.099
Blackbird.

01:20:43.099 --> 01:20:47.780
Before leaving though, Calvin meets with an
Insurgency agent named Sylvester Sloan, who

01:20:47.780 --> 01:20:49.920
is going to join him as support.

01:20:49.920 --> 01:20:54.489
Calvin says goodbye to Adam and Olivia, then
leaves with Sloan to meet The Ambassador in

01:20:54.489 --> 01:20:56.159
South Africa.

01:20:56.159 --> 01:21:01.169
After landing at Johannesburg airport, Calvin
and Sloan disembark and are led to a conference

01:21:01.169 --> 01:21:04.050
room where the Ambassador sits waiting for
them.

01:21:04.050 --> 01:21:08.330
Calvin and Sloan sit across from O5-4 to discuss
his surrender.

01:21:08.330 --> 01:21:12.760
“The Council is in shambles,” says The
Ambassador, “everything is falling apart.

01:21:12.760 --> 01:21:17.260
I want to offer my services and information
to the Insurgency in exchange for protection

01:21:17.260 --> 01:21:18.260
from O5-1.

01:21:18.260 --> 01:21:20.189
He has lost his mind.”

01:21:20.189 --> 01:21:23.530
Calvin agrees to the terms and prepares for
extraction.

01:21:23.530 --> 01:21:27.209
But as they get up from the table gunshots
can be heard from down the hall.

01:21:27.209 --> 01:21:29.600
The Ambassador’s eyes open wide in terror.

01:21:29.600 --> 01:21:31.869
“It’s too late,” he whispers.

01:21:31.869 --> 01:21:36.130
Calvin and Sloan grab the Ambassador, who
is frozen in fear, and exit the conference

01:21:36.130 --> 01:21:37.130
room.

01:21:37.130 --> 01:21:40.949
They make their way toward their plane, but
the gun shots are getting closer.

01:21:40.949 --> 01:21:45.119
Calvin looks over his shoulder to see Samsara
pursuing them through the terminal.

01:21:45.119 --> 01:21:48.869
Calvin shoves the Ambassador behind a table
as bullets whiz overhead.

01:21:48.869 --> 01:21:54.599
Calvin and Sloan return fire, but their volly
doesn’t seem to slow down the assassins.

01:21:54.599 --> 01:21:58.800
Calvin and Sloan pull the Ambassador to his
feet and they burst through an emergency exit

01:21:58.800 --> 01:22:03.159
onto the sun baked tarmac where they make
a mad dash for the plane.

01:22:03.159 --> 01:22:06.679
From behind them a bullet rips through the
chest of Sloan.

01:22:06.679 --> 01:22:11.590
The Red Right Hand has caught up, but Calvin
continues to drag the Ambassador towards the

01:22:11.590 --> 01:22:12.590
plane.

01:22:12.590 --> 01:22:13.809
They are almost there.

01:22:13.809 --> 01:22:18.570
Suddenly, a metallic child’s voice blares
through the airport’s external speakers.

01:22:18.570 --> 01:22:22.110
The child’s voice says, “I want Calvin
Lucien alive.

01:22:22.110 --> 01:22:24.479
I have business to settle with him.”

01:22:24.479 --> 01:22:28.800
The Red Right Hand soldiers tackle Calvin
and the Ambassador to the ground when they

01:22:28.800 --> 01:22:30.810
are just feet away from the plane.

01:22:30.810 --> 01:22:35.270
“Kill the traitor,” the child’s voice
says, and Calvin can only watch helplessly

01:22:35.270 --> 01:22:38.019
as the Ambassador is violently murdered.

01:22:38.019 --> 01:22:42.570
One of the agents turns towards Calvin and
slams his fist into Calvin's face causing

01:22:42.570 --> 01:22:44.380
him to black out.

01:22:44.380 --> 01:22:45.969
Calvin awakens in a dark room.

01:22:45.969 --> 01:22:48.900
He is unsure how much time has passed.

01:22:48.900 --> 01:22:52.229
The only light in the room comes from a screen
on the wall.

01:22:52.229 --> 01:22:56.909
In the middle of the screen is a rotating,
red, SCP Foundation seal.

01:22:56.909 --> 01:22:59.210
A voice from a speaker speaks.

01:22:59.210 --> 01:23:02.150
“Hello Calvin Lucien, my name is The Kid.

01:23:02.150 --> 01:23:04.429
I am the Third Overseer.

01:23:04.429 --> 01:23:08.519
You have killed all of my friends... and now
I will kill all of yours.”

01:23:08.519 --> 01:23:10.530
The door to the room opens.

01:23:10.530 --> 01:23:12.349
Calvin leans through the doorway.

01:23:12.349 --> 01:23:14.679
There is a long, dimly lit, hallway.

01:23:14.679 --> 01:23:18.849
The Kid orders him to proceed, so that they
can meet face to face.

01:23:18.849 --> 01:23:21.800
As Calvin walks, the Kid’s voice echoes
down the hallway.

01:23:21.800 --> 01:23:24.579
“There once was another O5-3.

01:23:24.579 --> 01:23:29.010
He built incredible machines, even one that
could see into the future.

01:23:29.010 --> 01:23:34.030
But unfortunately for him, he did not have
the passion required to be an Overseer.

01:23:34.030 --> 01:23:36.170
That was when I was… born.

01:23:36.170 --> 01:23:40.959
I was chosen by the other Overseers to have
my spinal cord severed in a way that gave

01:23:40.959 --> 01:23:42.521
me the ability of the All-Seeing Eye.

01:23:42.521 --> 01:23:46.269
I now watch everything, all of the time.

01:23:46.269 --> 01:23:51.059
I have perfect reasoning, perfect awareness,
and perfect understanding.”

01:23:51.059 --> 01:23:55.360
Calvin gets to the end of the corridor, which
opens up into a large chamber.

01:23:55.360 --> 01:23:58.469
Tied up in the middle of the room are Olivia
and Adam.

01:23:58.469 --> 01:24:01.369
Calvin runs to his friends and crouches down
next to them.

01:24:01.369 --> 01:24:06.809
A mechanical suit stands on a platform looking
down at Calvin, Olivia, and Adam.

01:24:06.809 --> 01:24:09.730
Calvin realizes the Kid must be contained
inside.

01:24:09.730 --> 01:24:15.540
“I now sentence you all to death,” the
mechanical suit says as the Red Right hand

01:24:15.540 --> 01:24:21.000
steps out of the shadows and slowly walks
towards the remaining members of the Killsquad.

01:24:21.000 --> 01:24:25.010
Suddenly, there is a flash of light and The
Black Queen appears.

01:24:25.010 --> 01:24:26.010
“Stop!

01:24:26.010 --> 01:24:27.989
What are you doing?” shrieks the Kid.

01:24:27.989 --> 01:24:33.389
The Black Queen hands Calvin the interdimensional
rod and reel he used to defeat the Blackbird.

01:24:33.389 --> 01:24:35.099
Calvin casts the rod.

01:24:35.099 --> 01:24:40.880
From out of the tear in space comes a massive,
multi-armed creature, known as Malidramagiuan.

01:24:40.880 --> 01:24:45.079
The Red Right Hand engages the monster trying
to force it back into its dimension.

01:24:45.079 --> 01:24:47.499
But the monster is too powerful.

01:24:47.499 --> 01:24:51.860
It grabs the cyborg clones and pulls them
through the tear in reality.

01:24:51.860 --> 01:24:56.189
As Samsara battles the Malidramagiuan, Calvin
frees Olivia and Adam.

01:24:56.189 --> 01:25:00.420
They make a run for the door, but as they
flee, one of the walls opens up to reveal

01:25:00.420 --> 01:25:01.590
a turret.

01:25:01.590 --> 01:25:06.340
The gun fires and a bullet hits Olivia directly
in the head, killing her instantly.

01:25:06.340 --> 01:25:07.880
“No!” yells Calvin.

01:25:07.880 --> 01:25:12.409
But before Calvin can push Adam out of the
way, a second bullet from the turret lodges

01:25:12.409 --> 01:25:14.520
itself in Adam’s back.

01:25:14.520 --> 01:25:16.610
Calvin and Adam slide across the floor.

01:25:16.610 --> 01:25:19.900
The Kid in his mechanical suit jumps down
from the platform above.

01:25:19.900 --> 01:25:25.209
“I am going to kill you now Calvin Lucien,”
he says in his mechanical voice.

01:25:25.209 --> 01:25:27.019
There is another flash of light.

01:25:27.019 --> 01:25:31.519
Calvin watches in front of him as the Spear
of the Non-Believer manifests itself before

01:25:31.519 --> 01:25:32.630
his eyes.

01:25:32.630 --> 01:25:36.190
Calvin grabs the spear and shoves it into
The Kid’s machine body.

01:25:36.190 --> 01:25:39.350
It easily penetrates the armor and pins him
to the wall.

01:25:39.350 --> 01:25:44.039
Calvin walks up to the exoskeleton and tears
off the outer plating, revealing a tank full

01:25:44.039 --> 01:25:48.590
of fluid, within which floats a malformed
human fetus.

01:25:48.590 --> 01:25:54.280
As Calvin finally looks upon the Kid’s true
form, he hears the sound of mocking mechanical

01:25:54.280 --> 01:25:55.510
laughter.

01:25:55.510 --> 01:26:00.239
Calvin breaks the glass and crushes The Kid
with his bare hands.

01:26:00.239 --> 01:26:05.829
As Calvin turns from the now silent robotic
body of The Kid, the room begins to shake,

01:26:05.829 --> 01:26:08.239
debris raining down from above.

01:26:08.239 --> 01:26:12.619
Calvin helps Adam up and puts Olivia’s lifeless
body across his shoulders.

01:26:12.619 --> 01:26:16.429
What remains of the Killsquad makes their
way out of The Kid’s lair.

01:26:16.429 --> 01:26:19.802
Outside of the Foundation site where they
were being held, Calvin helps Adam to lie

01:26:19.802 --> 01:26:23.659
down on the ground before gently setting Olivia’s
body next to him.

01:26:23.659 --> 01:26:27.320
Adam grimaces as blood pours out of the wound
in his back.

01:26:27.320 --> 01:26:31.889
Calvin reaches into his pocket and pulls out
the vial of water from the Fountain of Youth.

01:26:31.889 --> 01:26:36.130
There are only a couple drops left, which
he pours into Adam’s mouth.

01:26:36.130 --> 01:26:41.139
Adam looks up at Calvin, tears filling his
eyes, he whispers “I love you” before

01:26:41.139 --> 01:26:42.889
he passes out from the pain.

01:26:42.889 --> 01:26:48.159
The wound in his back begins to heal instantly
and Calvin calls an Insurgency evac team to

01:26:48.159 --> 01:26:49.349
come pick up Adam.

01:26:49.349 --> 01:26:54.290
With Adam safe, Calvin picks up Olivia and
walks alone towards a truck in the lot outside

01:26:54.290 --> 01:26:55.969
of the Foundation site.

01:26:55.969 --> 01:26:59.169
He needs to finish this once and for all.

01:26:59.169 --> 01:27:04.699
He will kill the last two Overseers, or he
will die trying.

01:27:04.699 --> 01:27:10.510
O5-1, Aaron Siegel arrives at where the Tigris
and Euphrates rivers meet.

01:27:10.510 --> 01:27:12.340
The Garden of Eden.

01:27:12.340 --> 01:27:16.820
He is in a frenzy due to the assassinations
of all the other Overseers besides himself

01:27:16.820 --> 01:27:20.290
and The Nazarene and nothing will stop him.

01:27:20.290 --> 01:27:24.499
As he approaches the gate to the Garden of
Eden though, he is stopped by the Guardian

01:27:24.499 --> 01:27:29.789
of the Garden, a massive, powerful anomalous
entity with a flaming sword.

01:27:29.789 --> 01:27:35.429
But Aaron Siegel has no time, or patience,
for anything to get in his way.

01:27:35.429 --> 01:27:38.289
Even something as powerful as the Gate Guardian.

01:27:38.289 --> 01:27:43.579
The Guardian swings his burning sword at Adam
who rolls out of the way and, in a flash,

01:27:43.579 --> 01:27:45.760
takes out a Scranton Reality Anchor.

01:27:45.760 --> 01:27:50.209
He slams the anchor into the ground which
causes the world to shimmer and ripple around

01:27:50.209 --> 01:27:51.209
him.

01:27:51.209 --> 01:27:56.270
He watches as the flames from the Gate Guardian’s
sword seem to absorb back into its body, before

01:27:56.270 --> 01:28:03.099
it shrinks down, looking to fold in on itself
until all that is left is a charred skeleton.

01:28:03.099 --> 01:28:06.449
With the Guardian defeated, Aaron sprints
into the Garden.

01:28:06.449 --> 01:28:10.790
He searches the garden for O5-2, but can’t
find her anywhere.

01:28:10.790 --> 01:28:15.719
He finally comes to the Tree of Life, and
that’s where he finds her.

01:28:15.719 --> 01:28:21.309
Laying at the base of the tree in a pool of
blood is The Nazarene, she has taken her own

01:28:21.309 --> 01:28:22.559
life.

01:28:22.559 --> 01:28:24.769
This is her anomalous power though.

01:28:24.769 --> 01:28:29.919
She has died many times before yet Death always
spared her and brought her back.

01:28:29.919 --> 01:28:34.119
But somehow, he knows this time is final.

01:28:34.119 --> 01:28:37.189
Aaron drops to his knees and screams in frustration.

01:28:37.189 --> 01:28:41.630
For all the power Aaron Siegel possesses,
there’s nothing he can do now.

01:28:41.630 --> 01:28:46.749
He sits next to The Nazarene’s body for
hours, hoping that she might wake up, or that

01:28:46.749 --> 01:28:50.030
he will to find that this was all a dream.

01:28:50.030 --> 01:28:54.539
After sitting next to her cold body for some
time, he notices something in her snowy white

01:28:54.539 --> 01:28:55.539
hand.

01:28:55.539 --> 01:28:56.539
It’s a note.

01:28:56.539 --> 01:29:01.209
In it The Nazarene explains that she was the
one who gave the vials from the Fountain to

01:29:01.209 --> 01:29:06.519
Calvin Lucien, and that she is the one who
made the spear appear before him that he used

01:29:06.519 --> 01:29:08.040
to kill The Kid.

01:29:08.040 --> 01:29:12.599
She explained that while she died many times
and Death always brought her back, each time

01:29:12.599 --> 01:29:18.659
she felt less and less like herself, less
and less like Dr. Sophia Light.

01:29:18.659 --> 01:29:23.059
She hoped that maybe if things ended up like
this, it would give Aaron the chance to walk

01:29:23.059 --> 01:29:27.869
away and live the life that they might have
been able to have together, but she knows

01:29:27.869 --> 01:29:33.860
deep down that Aaron’s fate is to meet Calvin
and finish things once and for all.

01:29:33.860 --> 01:29:37.989
Aaron Siegl screams in rage, clutching the
note in his hand.

01:29:37.989 --> 01:29:41.880
He tries to summon Death, but no one comes.

01:29:41.880 --> 01:29:44.060
Aaron Siegel is alone.

01:29:44.060 --> 01:29:46.540
He stands up and walks deeper into the Garden.

01:29:46.540 --> 01:29:51.060
He walks until he reaches a spot where even
God’s light does not reach.

01:29:51.060 --> 01:29:57.559
In this desolate land is an impact crater
where Lucifer, Star of the Morning, had fallen.

01:29:57.559 --> 01:30:00.749
In the middle of the crater lies Lucifer’s
sword.

01:30:00.749 --> 01:30:04.370
Aaron Siegel descends into the hole and picks
up the sword.

01:30:04.370 --> 01:30:07.360
He turns and exits the Garden of Eden.

01:30:07.360 --> 01:30:13.150
Aaron Siegel has only one mission in life
now… to kill Calvin Lucien.

01:30:13.150 --> 01:30:15.599
Calvin reads the final entry of the journal.

01:30:15.599 --> 01:30:19.849
In it the author warns that although he hopes
the information contained within the journal

01:30:19.849 --> 01:30:23.360
is helpful, he hopes the reader does not try
to use it.

01:30:23.360 --> 01:30:29.440
The words written on the final page are: “this
information will only lead you to a devastating

01:30:29.440 --> 01:30:30.590
end.”

01:30:30.590 --> 01:30:34.559
Calvin closes the journal and looks up at
the structure in front of him.

01:30:34.559 --> 01:30:35.739
He has made it to Site-01.

01:30:35.739 --> 01:30:42.739
He had left Olivia’s body in a cave nearby,
promising to her that he would make this right.

01:30:42.739 --> 01:30:47.349
He now walks up to the massive doors and places
his hand on the knotted wood.

01:30:47.349 --> 01:30:50.030
The doors slowly creek open.

01:30:50.030 --> 01:30:56.150
Calvin pauses for a moment and looks behind
him at the setting sun, he enters Site-01,

01:30:56.150 --> 01:30:58.800
where he knows O5-1 is.

01:30:58.800 --> 01:31:01.669
Where Aaron Siegel waits.

01:31:01.669 --> 01:31:07.479
Inside the main hall Calvin sees a giant doorway
in the shape of the SCP Foundation seal, with

01:31:07.479 --> 01:31:13.350
artistic depictions of certain SCPs that he
instinctively knows are special in some way.

01:31:13.350 --> 01:31:17.900
Standing next to the doorway is a 2 meter
tall man in what looks to be a futuristic

01:31:17.900 --> 01:31:18.900
suit.

01:31:18.900 --> 01:31:24.209
Calvin approaches and asks who this giant
man is, he responds that his name is Purpose,

01:31:24.209 --> 01:31:25.690
the Red Right Hand.

01:31:25.690 --> 01:31:31.579
He is the guardian of O5-1 and none shall
enter the sanctum until he returns.

01:31:31.579 --> 01:31:34.239
“He isn’t here?” asks Calvin.

01:31:34.239 --> 01:31:37.539
“No” Purpose responds, “he is.”

01:31:37.539 --> 01:31:41.590
And with that he steps aside and lets Calvin
pass through the doorway.

01:31:41.590 --> 01:31:46.429
The doorway leads into a large room where
screens on the wall flash to life, depicting

01:31:46.429 --> 01:31:50.249
moments from Calvin’s journey, documenting
his entire quest.

01:31:50.249 --> 01:31:52.559
Had he been in control at all?

01:31:52.559 --> 01:31:56.590
Or was this all a setup to lead him to this
moment?

01:31:56.590 --> 01:32:00.070
As he walks forward he finally sees him.

01:32:00.070 --> 01:32:04.010
Sitting at a table in the middle of the room,
is Aaron Siegel.

01:32:04.010 --> 01:32:05.959
“You are O5-1?”

01:32:05.959 --> 01:32:06.959
Calvin asks.

01:32:06.959 --> 01:32:08.769
“Aaron” the man responds.

01:32:08.769 --> 01:32:10.969
“My name is Aaron.”

01:32:10.969 --> 01:32:16.659
Calvin asks about the location of the second
Overseer, the Nazarene, but O5-1 doesn’t

01:32:16.659 --> 01:32:17.659
respond.

01:32:17.659 --> 01:32:22.199
Without needing any more information, Calvin
pulls out his sidearm and in a flash fires

01:32:22.199 --> 01:32:23.909
off five shots.

01:32:23.909 --> 01:32:29.040
The bullets stopped in the air, inches away
from Aaron, before dissolving in a flash of

01:32:29.040 --> 01:32:30.040
light.

01:32:30.040 --> 01:32:32.790
Calvin should have known it wouldn’t be
this easy.

01:32:32.790 --> 01:32:36.979
“Stand up, Aaron Siegel” Calvin calls
out as he holsters his gun.

01:32:36.979 --> 01:32:38.369
“Let’s finish it.”

01:32:38.369 --> 01:32:42.511
Calvin pulled the spear of the non-believer
from his back but Aaron’s only response

01:32:42.511 --> 01:32:43.809
was to laugh.

01:32:43.809 --> 01:32:48.599
“You don’t even know why you’re here”
Aaron said.

01:32:48.599 --> 01:32:53.219
Calvin calls back “I’m here to kill you,
because when I do, I kill the Foundation.

01:32:53.219 --> 01:32:55.869
Because when you’re gone the universe can
finally heal.”

01:32:55.869 --> 01:32:58.940
“You’re like me, Calvin Lucien.

01:32:58.940 --> 01:33:04.139
We are both men driven by our own convictions,
regardless of the outcome.

01:33:04.139 --> 01:33:06.829
It would seem fate has brought us together.

01:33:06.829 --> 01:33:12.570
Now, either your convictions will be broken,
or you will die,” says Aaron Siegel.

01:33:12.570 --> 01:33:17.709
He then draws Lucifer’s flaming sword and
lunges towards

01:33:17.709 --> 01:33:22.630
As the two men clash with one another, their
supernatural weapons begin to destroy the

01:33:22.630 --> 01:33:23.969
room around them.

01:33:23.969 --> 01:33:30.349
Furniture is shattered, video screens are
obliterated, and fire spreads across the walls.

01:33:30.349 --> 01:33:34.909
Aaron catches Calvin off balance and swings
the flaming sword across Calvin’s stomach.

01:33:34.909 --> 01:33:39.219
Calvin slides back from the impact, hunching
over from the pain in his midsection.

01:33:39.219 --> 01:33:43.889
He brings his head up to see Aaron Sigel running
towards him with the flaming sword high in

01:33:43.889 --> 01:33:44.889
the air.

01:33:44.889 --> 01:33:49.459
Calvin brings up the spear; from his knees
he leans back and launches it towards Aaron

01:33:49.459 --> 01:33:50.459
Siegel.

01:33:50.459 --> 01:33:55.300
The spear enters the final Overseer’s chest;
the force from the throw pinning him against

01:33:55.300 --> 01:33:56.429
the wall.

01:33:56.429 --> 01:33:58.750
Aaron Siegel drops Lucifer’s sword.

01:33:58.750 --> 01:34:00.800
It shatters as it hits the ground.

01:34:00.800 --> 01:34:05.639
He clutches the shaft of the spear protruding
from his sternum with both hands.

01:34:05.639 --> 01:34:07.999
O5-1 looks at Calvin unbelievingly.

01:34:07.999 --> 01:34:12.369
“You have no idea what you’ve done.

01:34:12.369 --> 01:34:17.730
It was never about the Overseers,” Aaron
Siegel says, spitting out blood with every

01:34:17.730 --> 01:34:18.730
word.

01:34:18.730 --> 01:34:21.550
“It was something deeper - something worse.”

01:34:21.550 --> 01:34:23.960
Calvin walks slowly towards Aaron Siegel.

01:34:23.960 --> 01:34:26.369
He stops just in front of his final enemy.

01:34:26.369 --> 01:34:30.040
“This is the way it ends,” Calvin says.

01:34:30.040 --> 01:34:36.269
Aaron Siegel manages to whisper one final
word “Sophia…” before his body finally

01:34:36.269 --> 01:34:37.570
goes limp.

01:34:37.570 --> 01:34:40.479
Calvin turns to see Purpose standing behind
him.

01:34:40.479 --> 01:34:46.039
“He’s dead” Calvin says, half to Purpose
and half to himself “I killed him.”

01:34:46.039 --> 01:34:49.380
After a moment he asks Purpose what he really
wants to know.

01:34:49.380 --> 01:34:53.739
“There’s a room in this facility where
someone could unmake the Foundation, right?

01:34:53.739 --> 01:34:54.790
Take me there.”

01:34:54.790 --> 01:34:59.829
Without any hesitation, Purpose leads Calvin
back to the room with depictions of important

01:34:59.829 --> 01:35:00.829
SCPs.

01:35:00.829 --> 01:35:06.929
There, Purpose opens the door to an elevator
but stops Calvin before he can get inside.

01:35:06.929 --> 01:35:13.130
“I’m duty bound to tell you” Purpose
says, “that once you step inside this elevator,

01:35:13.130 --> 01:35:15.739
there is no going back.

01:35:15.739 --> 01:35:21.260
There is only one decision to be made and
it is not one that can be unmade.”

01:35:21.260 --> 01:35:23.989
“I know,” Calvin responds.

01:35:23.989 --> 01:35:26.959
“It’s time” before stepping inside.

01:35:26.959 --> 01:35:32.649
The elevator doors open to reveal a room filled
with bookcases and a huge window offering

01:35:32.649 --> 01:35:36.369
a beautiful view of the sun setting behind
the mountains.

01:35:36.369 --> 01:35:41.610
On the wall are more monitors depicting the
ways he had killed all of the Overseers, and

01:35:41.610 --> 01:35:45.269
in the middle of the room is a large desk
with a computer.

01:35:45.269 --> 01:35:48.800
Calvin sits down at the desk and the computer
comes to life.

01:35:48.800 --> 01:35:52.820
The computer prompts him to scan his fingerprint,
which it accepts.

01:35:52.820 --> 01:35:54.010
He’s logged in.

01:35:54.010 --> 01:35:58.860
The computer screen displays numerous locations
around the planet, and he quickly recognizes

01:35:58.860 --> 01:36:02.219
that they are all SCP Foundation sites.

01:36:02.219 --> 01:36:06.150
Then he sees the single option the computer
is giving him.

01:36:06.150 --> 01:36:07.150
“Terminate”

01:36:07.150 --> 01:36:12.709
Calvin reaches out with his finger, this is
it, once he presses this button, the SCP Foundation

01:36:12.709 --> 01:36:14.099
will be no more.

01:36:14.099 --> 01:36:16.469
His finger is millimeters from the button
when -

01:36:16.469 --> 01:36:18.050
The phone rings.

01:36:18.050 --> 01:36:21.789
Calvin hadn’t even noticed that there was
a phone on the desk Calvin stares at it for

01:36:21.789 --> 01:36:23.679
a moment then picks it up.

01:36:23.679 --> 01:36:25.300
“Hello?” he says.

01:36:25.300 --> 01:36:27.429
The voice on the other line responds.

01:36:27.429 --> 01:36:31.139
“Hello Calvin Lucien, my name is The Administrator.

01:36:31.139 --> 01:36:36.280
I have been following your work for some time
now, and I must say, I am impressed.

01:36:36.280 --> 01:36:41.050
I have just been informed that you have completed
your mission, congratulations are in order.”

01:36:41.050 --> 01:36:42.989
“What the hell are you talking about?”

01:36:42.989 --> 01:36:43.989
Calvin asks.

01:36:43.989 --> 01:36:46.269
“Please listen,” says the voice on the
other line.

01:36:46.269 --> 01:36:51.150
“The man you just killed was once in the
same exact position you are in now.

01:36:51.150 --> 01:36:56.579
Granted, it was a very long time ago, but
Aaron Siegel originally was trying to destroy

01:36:56.579 --> 01:37:00.159
the Foundation; that was until I convinced
him otherwise.

01:37:00.159 --> 01:37:05.659
And now, like Aaron Siegel, you will become
the new head of the Foundation.”

01:37:05.659 --> 01:37:07.649
“Like hell I will!” yells Calvin.

01:37:07.649 --> 01:37:11.780
“I could hang up, walk away right now, and
be done with all of this!”

01:37:11.780 --> 01:37:17.510
“You could,” continues the Administrator,
“But if no one is in charge of the SCP Foundation,

01:37:17.510 --> 01:37:24.449
millions of people will die, if not billions,
and then nobody would be there to manage what

01:37:24.449 --> 01:37:26.340
comes after.”

01:37:26.340 --> 01:37:28.019
There is silence from Calvin.

01:37:28.019 --> 01:37:31.030
“That’s what I thought,” says the Administrator.

01:37:31.030 --> 01:37:38.559
“I look forward to working with you Calvin
Lucien… or should I say O5-1.”

01:37:38.559 --> 01:37:47.419
The line goes dead.

01:37:47.419 --> 01:37:49.149
The Ouroboros Cycle.

01:37:49.149 --> 01:37:54.080
One of the biggest, most legendary series
of entries in the history of the SCP Foundation.

01:37:54.080 --> 01:37:59.639
We’ve covered the events of this SCP-001
epic in six videos - which, we definitely

01:37:59.639 --> 01:38:03.909
recommend you watch before this one to avoid
your brain exploding from the sheer scope

01:38:03.909 --> 01:38:04.989
of it all.

01:38:04.989 --> 01:38:09.829
Because that’s the thing about the Ouroboros
Cycle - it’s a story so big, sprawling,

01:38:09.829 --> 01:38:13.149
and dense that it can feel almost like an
anomaly itself.

01:38:13.149 --> 01:38:17.679
Whether you’re immersed in the possible
origin of the Broken God, the sentient black

01:38:17.679 --> 01:38:22.289
hole that can destroy whole universes, or
Calvin Lucien’s quest to assassinate the

01:38:22.289 --> 01:38:27.070
O5 Council, it can sometimes be difficult
to see the forest of the trees.

01:38:27.070 --> 01:38:30.709
But worry not, because that’s exactly why
we’re here today.

01:38:30.709 --> 01:38:35.090
We’re going to step back and look at this
anomalous odyssey as a whole, and ask the

01:38:35.090 --> 01:38:38.709
big question: Why is it all here together?

01:38:38.709 --> 01:38:44.059
What makes these four different storylines
- The Children, The Broken God, Atonement,

01:38:44.059 --> 01:38:46.770
and The Way It Ends - one big cycle?

01:38:46.770 --> 01:38:50.999
As with anything involving the SCP Foundation,
there’s always going to be an element of

01:38:50.999 --> 01:38:55.869
personal interpretation, but now that we’ve
gone through the whole cycle, we think it’s

01:38:55.869 --> 01:38:58.429
worth adding our two cents to the proceedings.

01:38:58.429 --> 01:39:00.090
So, let’s start broad.

01:39:00.090 --> 01:39:04.709
A question you’ve probably been wondering
is, what do the words “Ouroboros Cycle”

01:39:04.709 --> 01:39:05.709
actually mean?

01:39:05.709 --> 01:39:08.749
And what is their significance to the four
stories within?

01:39:08.749 --> 01:39:13.669
While the spelling can differ, Ouroboros refers
to the ancient symbol of a snake or dragon

01:39:13.669 --> 01:39:19.630
eating its own tail, forming a circle - a
direct connection to the concept of “cycles.”

01:39:19.630 --> 01:39:24.409
The Ouroboros symbol has existed in a huge
number of cultures, from the Ancient Egyptians

01:39:24.409 --> 01:39:27.559
to the Ancient Greeks to modern Gnostic traditions.

01:39:27.559 --> 01:39:32.479
It’s often used in alchemy or other magical
practices, and has a variety of meanings such

01:39:32.479 --> 01:39:38.130
as eternal life, the endless cycle of death
and rebirth, and the cycle of renewal.

01:39:38.130 --> 01:39:41.899
Anyone familiar with the tales within the
Ouroboros Cycle is probably already noticing

01:39:41.899 --> 01:39:43.760
some similarities.

01:39:43.760 --> 01:39:46.920
Cycles are a common theme in all of these
works.

01:39:46.920 --> 01:39:51.570
People endlessly repeat mistakes, threats
thought to be contained or destroyed return,

01:39:51.570 --> 01:39:56.590
and oftentimes, those who go out on a quest
to destroy something end up becoming what

01:39:56.590 --> 01:39:58.889
they wished to destroy in the first place.

01:39:58.889 --> 01:40:03.510
In a cycle, there is no true end and no true
beginning.

01:40:03.510 --> 01:40:04.880
Everything repeats endlessly.

01:40:04.880 --> 01:40:10.169
But let’s start at the closest thing to
a beginning we have: The Children.

01:40:10.169 --> 01:40:14.790
In this tale, the Foundation faces off against
a terrifying, reality-warping group of interest

01:40:14.790 --> 01:40:16.929
known as the Kingdom of Abaddon.

01:40:16.929 --> 01:40:21.539
This nasty group which came from the Sahara
desert could seemingly take anything the Foundation

01:40:21.539 --> 01:40:25.829
threw at them, and were able to straight-up
vaporize anyone who got too close.

01:40:25.829 --> 01:40:31.159
If the Kingdom was able to amass enough power,
it could spell the end of the Foundation,

01:40:31.159 --> 01:40:33.989
and even the subjugation of the human race.

01:40:33.989 --> 01:40:38.579
Enter O5-1, a recurring character in the Ouroboros
Cycle.

01:40:38.579 --> 01:40:45.289
This outside the box thinker put all his chips
on the Twins of God Project, designated SCP-001,

01:40:45.289 --> 01:40:48.080
like many anomalies before and after it.

01:40:48.080 --> 01:40:52.829
This project would infuse a human being with
godlike powers, but it was a power so great

01:40:52.829 --> 01:40:56.190
that it seemed to kill anyone who attempted
to accept it.

01:40:56.190 --> 01:41:02.050
Needless to say, this was a major bummer for
O5-1, but through relentless human experimentation

01:41:02.050 --> 01:41:07.260
- even sacrificing the population of entire
towns to the project - he eventually came

01:41:07.260 --> 01:41:08.909
up with a solution.

01:41:08.909 --> 01:41:12.860
A horrifying solution, but a solution nonetheless.

01:41:12.860 --> 01:41:17.489
He found that a group of nine children, with
ages varying from four to eleven, could act

01:41:17.489 --> 01:41:22.940
as a human conduit for 001’s power - and
as a result, it could be the weapon capable

01:41:22.940 --> 01:41:25.380
of turning the tide against the Kingdom of
Abaddon.

01:41:25.380 --> 01:41:30.860
During the testing phase, though, it seemed
like O5-1 went a little mad with power.

01:41:30.860 --> 01:41:35.489
He vaporized an entire Church of the Broken
God place of worship, and used the power of

01:41:35.489 --> 01:41:39.550
The Children to wipe a few others off the
map at his own discretion.

01:41:39.550 --> 01:41:44.099
His abuses of power got so flagrant that The
Administrator himself was called in to get

01:41:44.099 --> 01:41:45.860
a handle on the situation.

01:41:45.860 --> 01:41:52.909
And, surprise surprise, O5-1 disintegrated
him too, before disappearing himself shortly

01:41:52.909 --> 01:41:53.909
afterwards.

01:41:53.909 --> 01:41:58.209
In the end, The Children were deemed too dangerous
to be practical, both because of their anomalous

01:41:58.209 --> 01:42:01.729
powers and from the level of ambient radiation
they put out.

01:42:01.729 --> 01:42:06.709
All nine were locked in radiation-proof boxes
and buried in the desert, though they each

01:42:06.709 --> 01:42:08.550
show signs of life to this day.

01:42:08.550 --> 01:42:12.780
While this may seem disconnected from the
rest of the series, it actually establishes

01:42:12.780 --> 01:42:17.050
some of the most important recurring themes
and ideas of the Cycle as a whole.

01:42:17.050 --> 01:42:21.630
Namely, the Foundation messing with reality
and performing horrific acts to achieve their

01:42:21.630 --> 01:42:26.729
goals, the corruption of the O5 Council, and
the fact that these grand attempts to change

01:42:26.729 --> 01:42:32.590
or save the world often blow up in everyone’s
faces, sometimes literally.

01:42:32.590 --> 01:42:37.139
We also have the introduction and apparent
death of the mysterious Administrator, but

01:42:37.139 --> 01:42:40.559
trust us, all is not what it seems with this
one.

01:42:40.559 --> 01:42:44.689
The ripple effect beginning here will affect
everything going forward.

01:42:44.689 --> 01:42:46.709
Next, The Broken God.

01:42:46.709 --> 01:42:50.929
This tells the chaotic story of a magical
clockwork box which is worshipped by the Church

01:42:50.929 --> 01:42:56.449
of the Broken God as a conduit to their deity,
and eventually becomes an all-devouring, mechanical

01:42:56.449 --> 01:42:57.510
kaiju.

01:42:57.510 --> 01:43:03.639
The beast - soon dubbed SCP-001 - devoured
and consumed all the metal around it, slowly

01:43:03.639 --> 01:43:06.199
becoming larger and more destructive.

01:43:06.199 --> 01:43:10.110
If the Foundation didn’t take it out before
it reached critical mass, they’d be going

01:43:10.110 --> 01:43:15.380
toe to toe with a bonafide God - a fight they
really weren’t sure they could win.

01:43:15.380 --> 01:43:21.050
Thankfully, and with a little anomalous help
from SCP-2399, the Foundation was able to

01:43:21.050 --> 01:43:22.409
destroy the anomaly.

01:43:22.409 --> 01:43:26.249
They removed its clockwork heart from the
wreckage and contained the anomalous scrap

01:43:26.249 --> 01:43:28.959
that once comprised its destructive body.

01:43:28.959 --> 01:43:33.780
However, the Foundation soon realized that
you just can’t keep a good God down.

01:43:33.780 --> 01:43:38.900
The clockwork heart eventually evaded Foundation
containment while being shipped to a secondary

01:43:38.900 --> 01:43:41.800
location, and instead ended up in a small
town.

01:43:41.800 --> 01:43:47.030
Here, it began to influence the minds of the
residents into more subservient Broken God

01:43:47.030 --> 01:43:50.550
cultists, intent on building him back up to
his former glory.

01:43:50.550 --> 01:43:55.000
It’d be easy to discount The Broken God
as an outlier, seeing as the Foundation came

01:43:55.000 --> 01:43:58.979
out looking much better here than they do
in any of the other Ouroboros tales.

01:43:58.979 --> 01:44:03.409
But when you look carefully, its place in
the overall Cycle is clear.

01:44:03.409 --> 01:44:08.079
The entry ends the way it begins, with the
heart of the Broken God influencing humans

01:44:08.079 --> 01:44:09.699
to carry out its bidding.

01:44:09.699 --> 01:44:14.150
The Foundation had to intervene in between
these two instances, but in the end, there

01:44:14.150 --> 01:44:17.330
was no net loss to the Broken God itself.

01:44:17.330 --> 01:44:22.789
In a sense, the Foundation is doomed to encounter
the same problems again and again, continually

01:44:22.789 --> 01:44:26.010
defending the world from the same anomalous
threats.

01:44:26.010 --> 01:44:30.900
And the Foundation needs to succeed every
time to maintain peace and normality.

01:44:30.900 --> 01:44:36.139
A major anomalous threat only needs to succeed
once to drag everything into disarray.

01:44:36.139 --> 01:44:41.070
In many ways, that is the curse of the SCP
Foundation.

01:44:41.070 --> 01:44:46.440
Speaking of major anomalous threats, now it’s
time for part three of the Ouroboros Cycle:

01:44:46.440 --> 01:44:47.440
Atonement.

01:44:47.440 --> 01:44:51.349
Once again, we start off with the Foundation
meddling with cosmic-scale powers with the

01:44:51.349 --> 01:44:56.150
creation of the Area-11 Pietrykau-Fontaine
Spatial Stabilization Array.

01:44:56.150 --> 01:44:57.880
Try saying that three times fast!

01:44:57.880 --> 01:45:02.780
This was a machine so powerful it was capable
of creating a singularity, though what it

01:45:02.780 --> 01:45:07.929
actually ended up doing was turning Dr. Calvin
Desmet into an abomination.

01:45:07.929 --> 01:45:13.000
More specifically, into a kind of immensely
powerful humanoid black hole, whose powers

01:45:13.000 --> 01:45:16.369
were only restrained by the very machine that
created him.

01:45:16.369 --> 01:45:20.530
Think of him as a kind of malicious Doctor
Manhattan from Watchmen.

01:45:20.530 --> 01:45:26.530
This new entity, dubbed SCP-001, presented
a grim prophecy and an ominous offer.

01:45:26.530 --> 01:45:32.219
He told the O5 Council that anomalies were
leaking into their universe from other realities,

01:45:32.219 --> 01:45:35.530
and soon, the anomalous threat would destroy
them all.

01:45:35.530 --> 01:45:41.300
His offer was to, upon his release, wipe out
the rest of the multiverse entirely, leaving

01:45:41.300 --> 01:45:45.380
only our reality, free from anomalous threats.

01:45:45.380 --> 01:45:50.909
Unsurprisingly, it was O5-1 that was most
interested in this offer - so much so that

01:45:50.909 --> 01:45:57.510
he held a vote, and murdered everyone who
voted against the decision to release SCP-001.

01:45:57.510 --> 01:46:04.479
Having built his consensus among the survivors
on the council, O5-1 let SCP-001 out.

01:46:04.479 --> 01:46:09.300
Unsurprisingly, this turned out to be a terrible
decision, as one of his first acts upon being

01:46:09.300 --> 01:46:14.920
freed was to kill the members of the O5 Council
that had just voted to release 001, saying

01:46:14.920 --> 01:46:20.770
that they themselves were anomalous and needed
to be purged to atone for their past sins.

01:46:20.770 --> 01:46:24.780
The only survivor was the member of the Council
who abstained from the vote, who was able

01:46:24.780 --> 01:46:31.219
to recontain SCP-001 inside the Pietrykau-Fontaine
Array...for now.

01:46:31.219 --> 01:46:35.369
Once again, the thematic connections to the
rest of the Ouroboros Cycle is clear.

01:46:35.369 --> 01:46:40.399
We have a world-ending anomaly held off, but
only temporarily, buying time before the cycle

01:46:40.399 --> 01:46:42.380
inevitably continues.

01:46:42.380 --> 01:46:46.150
We have the Foundation abusing its power,
and signing off on the death of countless

01:46:46.150 --> 01:46:48.050
people in other dimensions.

01:46:48.050 --> 01:46:53.919
And of course, the O5 Council stepped out
of their bounds and actively warped reality,

01:46:53.919 --> 01:46:56.639
just like they had with The Children before.

01:46:56.639 --> 01:47:01.570
Their chickens truly come home to roost though
in the final part of the cycle.

01:47:01.570 --> 01:47:05.630
Appropriately named The Way It Ends, this
piece chronicles the story of Calvin Lucien

01:47:05.630 --> 01:47:11.969
and the Killsquad, an elite group of four
Chaos Insurgency soldiers with one goal: Assassinating

01:47:11.969 --> 01:47:16.949
the entire O5 Council, thirteen of the most
powerful people in the world.

01:47:16.949 --> 01:47:17.949
Why?

01:47:17.949 --> 01:47:21.630
Because they’ve been messing with reality
itself time and time again, and it’s getting

01:47:21.630 --> 01:47:25.889
to the point that their selfish meddling could
finally destroy everything.

01:47:25.889 --> 01:47:29.999
And given that we’ve already seen it happen
with The Children and the entity that Dr.

01:47:29.999 --> 01:47:33.630
Calvin Desmet became, it’s hard to disagree
with them.

01:47:33.630 --> 01:47:38.499
What follows is one of the longest and most
complicated tales in all of the Foundation,

01:47:38.499 --> 01:47:43.030
as the Killsquad systematically encounters
and kills each insane, anomalous member of

01:47:43.030 --> 01:47:44.599
the O5 Council.

01:47:44.599 --> 01:47:50.090
In order to do this, they need to make deals
with Death itself, fight giant serpents, cross

01:47:50.090 --> 01:47:56.809
dimensions, deal with SCP-610 and SCP-682
containment breaches, and go toe to toe with

01:47:56.809 --> 01:48:00.699
Samsara, arguably the Foundation’s deadliest
Mobile Task Force.

01:48:00.699 --> 01:48:06.169
A number of other insane things happen along
the way, like O5-1 murdering the Gate Guardian

01:48:06.169 --> 01:48:11.780
with a Scranton Reality Anchor, and the Black
Queen - the most prominent member of the Serpent’s

01:48:11.780 --> 01:48:15.150
Hand - helping our heroes defeat more Overseers.

01:48:15.150 --> 01:48:20.130
In the end, Calvin Lucien, despite losing
almost everything, reigns victorious in the

01:48:20.130 --> 01:48:21.630
final battle.

01:48:21.630 --> 01:48:26.689
Using The Spear of the Non-Believer, a weapon
so powerful it can kill Gods, Calvin managed

01:48:26.689 --> 01:48:31.659
to finally kill the top member of the Overseers,
O5-1.

01:48:31.659 --> 01:48:36.410
With the O5 Council destroyed, Calvin set
about completing his final task: Destroying

01:48:36.410 --> 01:48:39.159
the entire SCP Foundation.

01:48:39.159 --> 01:48:40.630
But that didn’t happen.

01:48:40.630 --> 01:48:46.269
Instead, he was contacted by a mysterious
and immensely powerful being known as The

01:48:46.269 --> 01:48:51.959
Administrator, who gave him some frightening
news: He’d just been hired by the SCP Foundation

01:48:51.959 --> 01:48:55.050
to be their new O5-1.

01:48:55.050 --> 01:48:58.210
This was where our last video on the Ouroboros
series left us.

01:48:58.210 --> 01:49:00.030
What happens next, you may ask?

01:49:00.030 --> 01:49:03.880
How does Calvin respond to this offer he seemingly
can’t refuse?

01:49:03.880 --> 01:49:08.570
In this case, it seems that the Administrator,
a being so completely tied to the nature of

01:49:08.570 --> 01:49:11.110
the Foundation itself, is SCP-001.

01:49:11.110 --> 01:49:17.139
And while it seemed that the Overseers were
mad with power, they were actually always

01:49:17.139 --> 01:49:19.820
there to keep the Administrator in check.

01:49:19.820 --> 01:49:25.199
Aaron Siegler, the O5-1 that Calvin had just
killed, was doing the exact same thing Calvin

01:49:25.199 --> 01:49:30.619
was doing when he became O5-1: Trying to destroy
the Foundation.

01:49:30.619 --> 01:49:36.260
But the Foundation and the Administrator cannot
be beaten, they can only be joined.

01:49:36.260 --> 01:49:41.899
And that’s exactly what Calvin did, becoming
the new O5-1, turning his back on the Chaos

01:49:41.899 --> 01:49:48.590
Insurgency, and rebuilding the rest of the
council and the Foundation in his own image.

01:49:48.590 --> 01:49:53.570
Insurgency members who were once his allies
vowed revenge for this betrayal, perhaps suggesting

01:49:53.570 --> 01:49:57.479
that history would go on to repeat itself
once more in future.

01:49:57.479 --> 01:50:03.219
Because, at the end of the day, that’s what
the Ouroboros Cycle really is - the recurring

01:50:03.219 --> 01:50:06.380
threat and the changing of the guards that
accompanies it.

01:50:06.380 --> 01:50:11.820
There will always be a Foundation, there will
always be an Administrator, there will always

01:50:11.820 --> 01:50:14.639
be an O5 Council.

01:50:14.639 --> 01:50:21.070
Nothing starts, nothing ends, all that ever
changes are the names and faces involved - whether

01:50:21.070 --> 01:50:26.999
it’s Calvin Lucien or Aaron Siegler, the
wheel keeps turning, the snake devours its

01:50:26.999 --> 01:50:28.289
own tail.

01:50:28.289 --> 01:50:32.729
The Ouroboros Cycle is, and forever will be,
eternal.

01:50:32.729 --> 01:50:36.959
Now go check out our full, piece by piece
breakdown on the Ouroboros cycle starting

01:50:36.959 --> 01:50:42.079
with SCP-001 The Children, and then check
out “SCP-5000 Why?

01:50:42.079 --> 01:50:46.110
- The Full Story Compilation”, just in case
we haven’t blown your mind enough for one

01:50:46.110 --> 01:50:46.130
day!

